hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6001","And from Al-Awzai, he said: A man narrated to me, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is jealous, and the believer is jealous, and Allah's jealousy is that the servant commits what He has forbidden him."
"6002","And from Al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede Ramadan by a day or two days, except a man who used to fast a fast, then let him fast it."
"6003","And from Al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, Abu Hurairah narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prophet nor ruler but he has two confidants: a confidant who enjoins good upon him and forbids him evil, and a confidant who spares him no corruption; so whoever is shielded from its evil has been shielded, and he is of whichever of the two overcomes him."
"6004","And from Al-Awzai, from Az-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman and Sulayman ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jews and Christians do not dye, so oppose them."
"6005","And from Al-Awzai, he said: Abu Kathir narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wine is from these two trees: the date-palm and the grapevine."
"6006","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Jews and Christians do not dye, so oppose them."
"6007","Amr An-Naqid narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sulaym Ar-Raqqi narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Saad narrated to us, from Uqayl ibn Khalid, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has refuse, and the refuse of the mosque is: No, by Allah, and Yes, by Allah."
"6008","Abu Ibrahim At-Tarjuman narrated to us, Ubays ibn Maymun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any wailing woman who dies before repenting, Allah will clothe her in a garment of tar, and raise her before the people on the Day of Resurrection."
"6009","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq ibn Asma narrated to us, Ubays ibn Maymun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath, it is as he said: if he says: I am a Jew, then he is a Jew; and if he says: I am a Christian, then he is a Christian; and if he says: I am a Magian, then he is a Magian."
"6010","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil and Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, both saying: Abd Ar-Razzaq narrated to us, Bishr ibn Rafi Al-Harithi informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is naive and generous, and the wicked one is cunning and base."
"6011","Ahmad ibn Janab narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Al-Hajjaj ibn Furafisah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is naive and generous, and the wicked one is cunning and base."
"6012","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Abd Ar-Rahman ibn Amr Al-Awzai and Saeed ibn Yusuf narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in the funeral prayer: O Allah, forgive our living, our dead, our present, our young, our old. O Allah, whomever You keep alive, keep him alive upon Islam, and whomever You take from us, take him upon faith. O Allah, do not deprive us of his reward, and do not lead us astray after him."
"6013","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Suwayd, meaning Abu Hatim, narrated to us, he said: A companion of mine narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he prayed over the dead he would say: O Allah, forgive our living, our dead, our present, our absent, our young, our old, our males, our females; whomever You keep of us, keep him upon Islam, and whomever You take, take him upon faith."
"6014","Abd Al-Ala ibn Hammad An-Narsi narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Amir narrating, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Jews say that coitus interruptus is the minor female infanticide, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jews have lied, the Jews have lied; had Allah willed to create it, no withdrawal could prevent it."
"6015","Mahmud ibn Khidash narrated to us, Abbad ibn Al-Awwam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tribulation continues to afflict the believing man and believing woman: in his body, his wealth, and his child, until he meets Allah with no sin upon him."
"6016","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Abd Ar-Rahman Al-Awzai narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A previously married woman is not married until she is asked permission, nor is a virgin married until she is consulted, and her permission is silence."
"6017","Abdullah ibn Ar-Rumi narrated to us, Abd Ar-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, and the likeness of one who spends upon them is like one stretching out his hand with charity."
"6018","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd Al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The truest word spoken by the Arabs is the saying of Labid:"
"6019","Zuhayr narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Salamah, he said: I know it only from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran was revealed upon seven letters, and disputation about the Quran is disbelief - three times - what you recognize of it, act upon it, and what you are ignorant of, refer it to its knower."
"6020","Ibrahim ibn Saeed narrated to us, Abu Al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from Az-Zuhri, Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman informed me, that he heard Hassan ibn Thabit Al-Ansari adjuring Abu Hurairah: I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Hassan, respond on behalf of the Messenger of Allah; O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit. Abu Hurairah said: Yes."
"6021","Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor Muslims will enter Paradise five hundred years before their rich."
"6022","Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The orphan girl is to be consulted about herself; if she remains silent, then that is her consent."
"6023","'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah; and Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fasting person has two joys: a joy in this world at his breaking of the fast, and a joy in the Hereafter."
"6024","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, the brother of Hajjaj, narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change the white hair and do not resemble the Jews."
"6025","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Adhrami narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Abi Khath'am al-Yamami, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays six rak'ahs after Maghrib, not speaking any evil between them, it will be counted for him as the worship of twelve years."
"6026","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah did not send any Prophet, nor was there any caliph after him - I think he said - except that he had two confidants: a confidant who commands him to good and forbids him evil, and a confidant who spares him no corruption; so whoever is guarded from evil has been guarded."
"6027","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The days of Mina are days of eating and drinking."
"6028","Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: People will stand before the Lord of the worlds for the measure of half a day of fifty thousand years, and that Day will be made easy for the believer like the sun declining toward setting until it sets."
"6029","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The soul of the believer is suspended by his debt until it is settled on his behalf."
"6030","'Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah and Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is one of you incapable? For one to take a rope, gather firewood, eat from it and give charity is better for him than to ask people, whether they give him or withhold."
"6031","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyabi narrated to us, he said: Anas narrated to me, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, that he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah informed me that Abu Hurayrah heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: An ant bit a Prophet among the Prophets, so he ordered the village of ants and it was burned; then Allah revealed to him: Was it because one ant bit you that you destroyed a nation among the nations that glorifies Allah?"
"6032","Kamil ibn Talhah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he intended to prostrate, would say the takbir and then prostrate, and when he rose from sitting, would say the takbir and then stand."
"6033","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: He forbade hastening (to fast) a day or two before Ramadan."
"6034","'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A nation of the Children of Israel was lost; it is not known what happened to it, and I do not think it is but the mouse. Have you not seen that when camel's milk is brought near to it, it does not drink, but when sheep's milk is brought near to it, it drinks it? Abu Hurayrah said: So I narrated this hadith to Ka'b, and he said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said it to him repeatedly. Abu Hurayrah said: Then has the Torah been revealed to me?"
"6035","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whom do you count as the raqub among you? They said: The one who has no child. He said: No; rather it is the one who has no farat (a child who died before him)."
"6036","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man supplicating with both his fingers together, so he forbade him and said: With one of them, with the right one."
"6037","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sarf: a dirham for two dirhams; and Abu Bakr, and 'Umar, and 'Uthman (did likewise)."
"6038","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a prostitute woman saw a dog on a hot day circling a well, its tongue hanging out from thirst, so she removed her sock for it, and she was forgiven."
"6039","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is invited, let him respond; if he is fasting, let him supplicate, and if he is not fasting, let him eat."
"6040","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If ten of the Jews had followed me and believed in me, every Jew would have submitted. He said: Ka'b said: Twelve; the confirmation of that is in al-Ma'idah: And Allah took the covenant of the Children of Israel and We sent among them twelve chiefs."
"6041","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats or drinks forgetfully, it is but a provision that Allah provided him."
"6042","Muslim ibn Abi Muslim al-Jarmi narrated to us, Makhlad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibrahim did not tell a lie except for three lies, all of them for the sake of Allah: his saying, Indeed I am sick, and his saying, Rather the biggest of them did it. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibrahim, peace be upon him, set out traveling in the land of a tyrant among the tyrants, and with him was Sarah, and she was among the most beautiful of women. Word reached the tyrant that in your domain there is a man with a woman the onlookers have never seen any more beautiful than her, so he sent to him, and he came to him, and he asked him about the woman: Who is the woman with you? He said: My sister. He said: Then send her to me. So he sent a messenger with her, and he came to her and said: This tyrant asked me about you, and I told him you are my sister - and you are my sister in Islam - and he asked me to send you to him, so go to him; for Allah will withhold him from you. He said: So she went to him with his messenger, and when he brought her in to him, he lunged toward her, but was held back from her. He said to her: Supplicate to the God you worship to release me, and I will not return to what you dislike. So she supplicated to Allah and he was released, and he did that three times. Then he said to the one who had brought her: Take her out from me; for you did not bring me a human, you only brought me a devil. So he gave Hajar to her as a servant, and she returned to Ibrahim, and he asked her for her, and she gave her to him. Muhammad said: So she is your mother, O sons of the water of the sky, meaning the Arabs."
"6043","Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Bilal, and he brought out to him heaps of dates. He said: What is this, O Bilal? He said: Dates I stored, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Did you not fear that you would hear for it a sizzling in Hell? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear any reduction from the Owner of the Throne."
"6044","And from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to divide sheep among his Companions from the charity, with one sheep falling between two men, and one of them would say: Leave me your share so I may marry with it."
"6045","Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in his prayer and a need presents itself to him, then tasbih is for men and clapping is for women."
"6046","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak and 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man pray with his hands on his waist."
"6047","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, 'Abdah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Labid, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A woman entered the Fire because of a cat she tied up; she neither fed it nor gave it water, nor released it to eat from the vermin of the earth, until it died in its bond."
"6048","Repeated. And a prostitute entered Paradise: she passed by a dog at a well wanting water but unable to reach it, thirsty, so she removed her shoe - or her light boot - and tied it in her waist-wrapper or her headscarf, then drew water for it and gave it drink until it was quenched."
"6049","Abu Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out while we were disputing about the Decree, and he became angry until his face reddened, as if pomegranate seeds had been burst upon his face. Then he turned to us and said: Is this what you were commanded? Is this what I was sent to you with? Those before you perished only when they disputed about this matter. I adjure you not to dispute about it."
"6050","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whom do you count as the raqub among you? They said: The one who has no child. He said: Rather he is the one who has no farat."
"6051","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, Qurrah narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prostrated at When the sky is split open, as did Abu Bakr, and 'Umar, and one better than them; and he prostrated at Read in the name of your Lord, as did Abu Bakr, and 'Umar, and one better than them."
"6052","'Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh al-'Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, 'Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not swear by your fathers, nor by your mothers, nor by rivals (to Allah), and do not swear by Allah except while you are truthful."
"6053","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, that Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to him, that Abu Hurayrah narrated to him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning the musarrah: when a man buys it and milks it, he has the choice; if he wishes he keeps it, and if he wishes he returns it along with a sa' of dates."
"6054","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, that Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to him, that Abu Hurayrah narrated to him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that the goring animal is without liability, the mine is without liability, the well is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"6055","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: A man was forgiven for removing a branch from the road."
"6056","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reviling the believer is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."
"6057","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man called out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: When Allah gives you abundance, then be abundant upon yourselves. A man gathered his clothes upon himself; a man prayed in a waist-wrapper and a cloak, in a waist-wrapper and a shirt, in trousers and a long coat, in trousers and a cloak, in briefs and a long coat; he said: and I think he said: in briefs and a cloak."
"6058","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam and Ghifar, and something of Muzaynah and Juhaynah - or something of Juhaynah and Muzaynah - are better with Allah - he said: I think he said: on the Day of Resurrection - than Asad, Ghatafan, Hawazin, and Tamim."
"6059","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Friday there is an hour that no Muslim standing in prayer asking Allah for good coincides with but He gives it to him; and he gestured with his hand, making it brief and small."
"6060","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: People will keep asking about knowledge until they say: This is Allah who created us, so who created Allah? He said: While he was holding the hand of a man, he said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth; a man asked me about it, and this is the second; or two men, and this is the third."
"6061","'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sarf: a dirham for two dirhams; and Abu Bakr, and 'Umar, and 'Uthman (did likewise)."
"6062","'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub and Habib and Hisham, from Muhammad, and Qatadah, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I was fasting, then I ate and drank forgetfully. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah fed you and gave you drink, then He made you fast."
"6063","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Shabab narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted pre-Islamic poetry except the qasidah of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt about the people of Badr, and the qasidah of al-A'sha about 'Amir and 'Alqamah."
"6064","'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Habib and Hisham and Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah - I think he said - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The mouse is Jewish, and it does not drink camel's milk."
"6065","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ziyad ibn al-Rabi' al-Yuhmadi narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mouse is transformed, and the sign of that is that it drinks sheep's milk and does not drink camel's milk."
"6066","Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us, 'Awn ibn Kahmas narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The best of the people of the east is 'Abd al-Qays."
"6067","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves by my name, and do not use my kunyah."
"6068","Abu Yasir 'Ammar al-Mustamli narrated to us, Yusuf ibn 'Atiyah narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin narrate from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A Prophet among the Prophets was on an expedition; he rested under a tree and an ant stung him. When he departed, he ordered what was under the tree to be burned. So Allah revealed to him: Why not a single ant?"
"6069","'Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, Ayyub and Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah - Hisham said - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever buys a musarrah has the choice for three days; if he wishes he returns it along with a sa' of dates, not samra."
"6070","'Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile time, for Allah is al-Dahr."
"6071","Salih ibn Malik narrated to us, Abu 'Ubaydah al-Naji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by al-Baqi' by a woman crouching over a grave weeping. He said to her: O female servant of Allah, fear Allah and be patient. She said: O servant of Allah, I am the grieving bereaved one. He said: O female servant of Allah, fear Allah and be patient. She said: O servant of Allah, had you been afflicted you would have excused me. He said: O female servant of Allah, fear Allah and be patient. She said: O servant of Allah, you have made yourself heard, so go away from me. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on, and a man among his Companions followed him and stood by the woman and said to her: What did the man who went say to you? She said: He said to me such-and-such. He said: Do you know him? She said: No. He said: That is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So she leapt up hastening, saying: I will be patient, I will be patient, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Patience is at the first shock; patience is at the first shock."
"6072","And with it from Abu Hurayrah, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a sick son of hers, and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to heal this son of mine. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Have you a farat? She said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: In the pre-Islamic time or in Islam? She said: Rather in Islam. He said: A strong shield, a strong shield, a strong shield."
"6073","Qasim ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn al-Hakam, from 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has taken a strong shield, whoever has three children precede him in Islam."
"6074","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: People are mines in good and evil; the best of them in the pre-Islamic time are the best of them in Islam when they understand."
"6075","Al-Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated to us, 'Imran ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets and eats or drinks, let him complete his fast, for Allah fed him and gave him drink."
"6076","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The goring animal's wound is without liability, the well is without liability, the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"6077","Zakariyya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the arriving caravans."
"6078","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell - or from the exhalation of the gates of Hell - so cool the prayer."
"6079","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The goring animal's wound is without liability, the well is without liability, the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"6080","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you urinate in standing water and then bathe from it."
"6081","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to the delegation of 'Abd al-Qays: I forbid you the naqir, the hantam, the dubba, the muzaffat, and the tied-up waterskin with its top cut off; but drink in your waterskin and tie it shut."
"6082","'Isa ibn Salim narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the arriving goods; if a person meets them and buys, the owner of the goods has the choice when he reaches the market."
"6083","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, 'Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: No two Muslims between whom three children die before reaching puberty but Allah admits them to Paradise by His abundant mercy to them. He said: It is said to them: Enter Paradise, and they say: Until our parents come. Then it is said to them: Enter Paradise, you and your parents."
"6084","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, which charity is greatest? He said: That you give charity while you are healthy and miserly, fearing poverty and hoping for life; and do not delay until, when it reaches the throat, you say: For so-and-so such, and for so-and-so such, though it already belonged to so-and-so."
"6085","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said the takbir in prayer, would pause briefly before reciting the Qur'an. I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, what do you say in your silence between the takbir and the recitation? He said: I say: O Allah, distance between me and my sins as You distanced between the east and the west; O Allah, purify me of my sins as the white garment is purified of filth; O Allah, wash me of my sins with water, snow, and hail."
"6086","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Who among people is most entitled from me to good companionship? He said: Your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your father."
"6087","And from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on his neck bellowing, saying: O Messenger of Allah; I say: I own nothing for you against Allah; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a sheep on his neck bleating, saying: O Messenger of Allah; I say: I own nothing for you against Allah; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a horse on his neck neighing, saying: O Messenger of Allah; I say: I own nothing for you against Allah; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a soul on his neck screaming, saying: O Messenger of Allah; I say: I own nothing for you against Allah; I have conveyed to you. And let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with silent wealth on his neck, saying: O Messenger of Allah; I say: I own nothing from Allah; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with fluttering papers on his neck, saying: O Messenger of Allah; I say: I own nothing from Allah; I have conveyed to you."
"6088","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first group to enter Paradise will be upon the form of the moon on the night of the full moon, and those who follow them upon the form of the brightest brilliant star in the sky in light. They do not urinate, nor defecate, nor blow their noses. Their combs are gold, their sweat is musk, their censers are aloeswood, and their wives are the wide-eyed houris. Their manners are upon one manner, upon the form of their father Adam, sixty cubits in the sky."
"6089","And from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until the sun rises from its west; when it rises and people see it, all those upon it will believe, when no soul will benefit from its faith that had not believed before, or earned good in its faith."
"6090","And with his isnad, from Abu Zur'ah he said: I and Abu Hurayrah entered a house being built in Madinah for Sa'id - or for Marwan - he said: Abu Hurayrah performed ablution and washed his hands until he reached his armpits, and washed his feet until he reached his knees. I said: What is this, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: It is the utmost of the ornament. He said: And he saw a painter painting in the house, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty said: Who is more unjust than one who goes to create like My creation! Let them create a grain, let them create an atom!"
"6091","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks people for their wealth in abundance is but asking for embers, so let him take little or much."
"6092","And from Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of wisal - three times - They said: O Messenger of Allah, you practice wisal. He said: You are not in that like me; I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink. Take upon yourselves of deeds what you can bear."
"6093","And from Abu Hurayrah he said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Khadijah coming to you with a vessel in it condiment, or food, or drink. When she comes to you, convey to her greeting from her Lord, and give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow reed with no noise in it nor toil."
"6094","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cat is a beast of prey."
"6095","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Talq ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A woman came with a boy of hers and said: O Prophet of Allah, supplicate to Allah, supplicate to Allah, for I have buried three. He said: You buried three? She said: Yes. He said: You have taken a strong guard against the Fire."
"6096","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Sharik ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' and Ibn Shubrumah, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me who among people is most entitled to good companionship? He said: Yes, by your father you will be informed: Your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your father. He said: Inform me, O Messenger of Allah, of wealth I may give as charity? He said: Yes, by Allah you will be informed: Give charity while you are healthy and miserly, hoping for life and fearing poverty; and do not delay until, when your soul is here and here, you say: My wealth is for so-and-so, and my wealth is for so-and-so, though it is theirs even if you dislike it."
"6097","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Abu Zur'ah narrate from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: My nation will perish at the hands of this tribe of Quraysh. They said: What do you command us? He said: If only people would keep away from them."
"6098","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from his father, from 'Umarah, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, who among people is most entitled from me to good companionship? He said: Your mother, then your father, then the nearest, the nearest."
"6099","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man has a station with Allah, which he does not reach by deed, so Allah keeps afflicting him with what he dislikes until He makes him reach it."
"6100","Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, 'Umarah narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two phrases, light on the tongue, beloved to the Merciful, heavy in the Scale: Glory be to Allah and with His praise; Glory be to Allah the Great."
"6101","Al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah ibn 'Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said the takbir toward prayer, would pause briefly before reciting. I said to him: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, what do you say in this silence of yours between the takbir and the recitation? He said: O Allah, distance between me and my sins as You distanced between the east and the west; O Allah, purify me of my sins as the white garment is purified of filth; O Allah, wash me of my sins with snow, water, and hail."
"6102","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id Abu Hayyan al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah ibn 'Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us one day and mentioned embezzlement, magnifying its matter. Then he said: O people, let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on his neck bellowing, saying: O Messenger of Allah, aid me; I say: I own nothing for you against Allah; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a sheep on his neck bleating, saying: O Messenger of Allah, aid me; I say: I own nothing for you against Allah; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a horse on his neck neighing, saying: O Messenger of Allah, aid me; I say: I own nothing for you against Allah; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a soul on his neck screaming, saying: O Messenger of Allah, aid me; I say: I own nothing for you against Allah; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with fluttering papers on his neck, saying: O Messenger of Allah, aid me; I say: I own nothing for you against Allah; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with silent wealth on his neck, saying: O Messenger of Allah, aid me; I say: I own nothing for you against Allah; I have conveyed to you."
"6103","'Uqbah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, that he narrated to them that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a sick son of hers, for him to supplicate for him for healing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying: If he dies, may Allah reward you in him. She said: I have sent forth three in Islam."
"6104","'Uqbah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah ibn 'Amr ibn Jarir, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant has a lofty station with Allah which he does not attain by deed, so Allah keeps afflicting him with what he dislikes until He makes him attain it."
"6105","Ahmad ibn 'Imran al-Akhnasi narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, he said: I entered with Abu Hurayrah the house of Marwan, and in it were statues. Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah Mighty and Majestic said: Who is more unjust than one who created a creation like Mine; let them create an atom, or create a grain, or create barley."
"6106","Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Salim, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves by my name, and do not use my kunyah."
"6107","'Abdullah ibn 'Awn narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, he said: I was informed from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make the provision of the family of Muhammad in this world sustenance."
"6108","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abu Hayyan, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bilal, what is the most hopeful deed you did of benefit in Islam? Bilal said: I did no deed in Islam more hopeful of benefit to me than that I never purified myself with a purification by night or day but I prayed with that purification for my Lord what was decreed for me to pray. He said: I heard tonight the movement of your sandals before me in Paradise."
"6109","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Jibril sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then looked at the sky and an angel was descending. Jibril said to him: This angel has not descended since he was created before this hour. When he descended, he said: O Muhammad, your Lord sent me to you: Shall I make you a king, or a servant messenger? Jibril said to him: Humble yourself to your Lord, O Muhammad. He said: No, rather a servant messenger."
"6110","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Waki' and Abu Usamah narrated to us, both said: Jarir ibn Ayyub al-Bajali narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah ibn 'Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd."
"6111","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dates for dates, wheat for wheat, salt for salt, like for like; whoever increases or seeks increase, it is usury, except what differs in kind."
"6112","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah; and Mughirah, from al-Harith al-'Ukli, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I shall never cease loving Banu Tamim after three things: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: They are the fiercest of my nation against the Dajjal. And 'A'ishah had a slave soul of the Banu Isma'il upon her, then captives of Khawlan arrived, and 'A'ishah said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not buy from them? He said: No. When captives of Bal'anbar arrived, he said: Buy, for they are the children of Isma'il. And charities of Banu Tamim came, and he said: These are the charities of our people."
"6113","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said the takbir in prayer, would be silent between the takbir and the recitation."
"6114","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Umarah, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the servants of Allah are servants whom the Prophets and the martyrs envy. It was said: Who are they? Perhaps we may love them. He said: They are a people who loved one another by the light of Allah, without kinship or lineage. Their faces are light upon pulpits of light. They do not fear when people fear, nor grieve when people grieve. Then he recited: Indeed the allies of Allah, no fear is upon them nor do they grieve."
"6115","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Yazid informed us, from Jarir ibn Yazid, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A hadd established in the land is better than forty mornings of rain."
"6116","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, Ibn Shubrumah narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No contagion, no evil omen, no hamah, no Safar. He said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, a scab of mange appears on the rump of a camel or its tail, then all of it becomes covered with mange? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who infected the first? Allah created every beast and wrote its provision, its death, and its term."
"6117","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: 'Uyaynah ibn Hisn al-Fazari entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him kissing Hasan or Husayn. He said: He said: O Messenger of Allah, ten have been born to me and I have kissed none of them. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"6118","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ar'arah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Abd al-Karim narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Samad ibn Ma'qil narrated to me that he heard Wahb addressing the people upon the minbar, saying: Remember from me three things: beware of followed desire, an evil companion, and a man's admiration of himself."
"6119","Ibrahim narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us that he heard Wahb say: Everything has two ends and a middle; when one end is held, the other inclines, but when you hold the middle, both ends balance. And he said: Keep to the middle courses of things."
"6120","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every predator with fangs, and the tied-up target, and the domestic donkey on the day of Khaybar."
"6121","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jews split into seventy-one - or seventy-two - sects, and the Christians split into seventy-one - or seventy-two - sects, and my nation will split into seventy-three sects."
"6122","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smelled an odor in the mosque and said: Whoever eats of this foul tree, let him not enter our mosque; meaning: garlic."
"6123","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out while Aslam were shooting, and said: Shoot, O sons of Isma'il; for your father was an archer. Shoot, and I am with Ibn al-Adra'. The people held back their bows and said: Whomsoever you are with prevails. He said: Shoot, and I am with all of you."
"6124","Abu Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists, and said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"6125","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Fire was shown to me, and I saw in it Ibn Qam'ah ibn Khindif dragging his intestines in the Fire. He was the first to let loose the sa'ibah and changed the covenant of Ibrahim. The one I saw most resembling him is Aktham ibn al-Jawn. He said: Aktham said: O Messenger of Allah, will his resemblance harm me? He said: No, you are a Muslim and he is a disbeliever."
"6126","Abu Musa narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Abi Khalifah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Satan confronted me in my prayer, so I seized him by the throat and throttled him; I could feel the coolness of his tongue upon the back of my hand. Had it not been for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, he would have been tied up in the morning for you to look at."
"6127","Abu Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fabricates against me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"6128","Abu Musa narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two sales in one sale, and two garments, and that a man sit with his knees drawn up with nothing between him and the sky, and that one of you wrap himself in the samma wrap upon one shoulder."
"6129","Abu Musa narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Abi Khalifah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he intended a journey, would cast lots among his wives; the lot fell to 'A'ishah in the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq."
"6130","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Mufaddal ibn Yunus, from al-Awza'i, from Abu Yasar al-Qurashi, from Abu Hashim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw an effeminate man who had dyed his feet with henna, and said: What is the matter with this? It was said: O Messenger of Allah, he imitates women. He said: He ordered concerning him, and he was banished to al-Naqi'. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we kill him? He said: I have been forbidden to kill those who pray. And al-Naqi' is a district in Madinah, and it is not al-Baqi'."
"6131","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Every weak one deemed weak, with two worn garments, to whom no heed is paid; if he swears by Allah, He fulfills it. Shall I not inform you of the people of the Fire? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Every coarse, arrogant, haughty one. He said: I said to Abu Hurayrah: What is al-jazz? He said: The bulky. He said: I said: What is al-ja'z? He said: The one great in his own self."
"6132","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Humayd al-Ru'asi ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh, and the muzaffat, and the dubba."
"6133","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Dharr, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to us, so we came and sought permission."
"6134","Bishr ibn Hilal al-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man fasts a day voluntarily, then is given the earth's fill of gold, he will not receive his full reward before the Day of Reckoning."
"6135","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Abu Maymunah: I witnessed Abu Hurayrah give a boy the choice between his father and his mother, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a boy the choice between his father and his mother."
"6136","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Khalid, from 'Abdullah ibn Rafi', the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and said: Allah created the soil on Saturday, created in it the mountains on Sunday, created the trees on Monday, created the disliked on Tuesday, created light on Wednesday, scattered beasts on Thursday, and created Adam after 'Asr on Friday, the last of creation at the last hour of the hours of Friday."
"6137","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Hassan ibn 'Atiyah, from Muhammad ibn Abi 'A'ishah, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you finishes the tashahhud, let him seek refuge with Allah from four: from the punishment of Hell, from the punishment of the grave, from the trial of life and death, and from the evil of the false Messiah, the Dajjal."
"6138","Hashim ibn al-Harith narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Ziyad ibn Abi al-Mughirah or Ziyad ibn al-Mughirah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they do it, they have protected their blood and wealth from me except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah. He said: And I heard him say: The guest has a right upon the one with whom he stays of three; what is beyond that is charity. And upon the guest is to depart without burdening the people of the house with sin. He said: And I heard him say, meaning: No Muslim supplicates with anything but it is answered for him in it: either He gives it to him, or He expiates thereby a sin from him, so long as he does not supplicate with sin or severing of kinship."
"6139","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, 'Abd al-Salam ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Abu Yazid al-Madini, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The runaway is to be returned; meaning: the runaway camel."
"6140","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Aban ibn 'Abdullah al-Bajali narrated to us, from a freedman of Abu Hurayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the privy, so I brought him water; he cleansed himself, wiped his hand with soil, then washed his hand."
"6141","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from 'Imran al-Qattan, from Abu Murayah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The angels do not invoke blessings upon a wailing woman nor upon one who trills (in wailing)."
"6142","Al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khuthaym ibn 'Irak ibn Malik, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: There is no charity in a Muslim's slave nor in his horse."
"6143","Al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar, from a man, from Makhul, from 'Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: There is no charity in horses and slaves except the charity of al-Fitr."
"6144","'Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me, from a cousin of Abu Hurayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, that Ma'iz ibn Malik came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery. He turned away from him until he said it four times; when it was the fifth time, he said: You committed adultery? He said: Yes. He said: And do you know what adultery is? He said: Yes, I came to her unlawfully what a man comes to his wife lawfully. He said: What do you want with this statement? He said: I want you to purify me. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you insert that of you into that of her, as the kohl-stick disappears into the kohl-container, and the staff into the thing? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So he ordered him stoned, and he was stoned. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard two men, one of them saying to his companion: Did you not see this one? Allah concealed him, but his soul would not leave him until he was stoned like the stoning of a dog?! Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled a little, then passed by the carcass of a donkey and said: Where are so-and-so and so-and-so? Dismount and eat of the carcass of this donkey. They said: May Allah forgive you, O Messenger of Allah, can this be eaten? He said: What you just took of your brother is a more severe eating than it. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, he is now in the rivers of Paradise plunging into them."
"6145","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Ibn Abi 'Adi and 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Mansur wrote it to me and I recited it to him, he said: Abu 'Uthman, the freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the occupant of this chamber, the truthful believed one, say: Mercy is not removed except from a wretched one."
"6146","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, he said: Thabit al-Zuraqi narrated to me, that Abu Hurayrah said: A wind seized people on the road to Makkah while 'Umar was on pilgrimage, and it intensified upon them. He said to those around him: What is the wind? Nothing was returned to him, and what 'Umar had asked about reached me. So I urged my mount until I caught up with him, and said: O Commander of the Believers, we were told you asked about the wind, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Wind is from the mercy of Allah; it comes with mercy and comes with punishment, so do not revile it; ask Allah for its good and seek refuge with Him from its evil."
"6147","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Sakan al-Basri narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Zibyan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has a choicest part, and the choicest part of prayer is the first takbir."
"6148","Al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning His saying: The Day We shall call every people by their leader: One of them is called and given his book in his right hand, his body is extended sixty cubits, his face is whitened, and a crown of pearl is placed on his head. He said: He proceeds to his companions, and they see him from afar and say: O Allah, bring us this one and bless us in this one, until he comes to them and says: Rejoice, for every man among you shall have this. As for the disbeliever, his book is given in his left hand, his face is blackened, his body is increased sixty cubits upon the form of Adam, and he wears a crown of Fire. His companions see him and say: We seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this one; O Allah, do not bring us this one. Then he comes to them, and they say: O Allah, keep him back. He says: May Allah keep you away, for every man among you shall have the like of this."
"6149","Muhammad ibn Qudamah narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi 'Ata, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies ill dies a martyr, is guarded from the two testers of the grave, and is brought morning and evening provision from Paradise."
"6150","He said: And Ibn Abi Rawwad and Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah al-Kilabi both narrated it to me, both said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"6151","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Dimam narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Increase in testifying that there is no god but Allah before you are barred from it."
"6152","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Dimam narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Exchange gifts, you will love one another."
"6153","And with it from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: O sons of Qusayy, O sons of Hashim, O sons of 'Abd Manaf, I am the warner, death is the raider, and the Hour is the appointment."
"6154","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever and headache keep afflicting the servant and the maidservant, though they bear sins like Uhud, and they do not leave them with even a mustard-seed's weight upon them."
"6155","'Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Qiran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, how incapable - or he said: how weak - is so-and-so? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You backbit your companion and ate his flesh."
"6156","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abdah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: A woman was punished for a cat she tied up; she did not let it eat from the vermin of the earth until it died."
"6157","Suwayd narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Hilal Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from al-Agharr, he said: I bear witness upon Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id that they bore witness upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Five, whoever says them Allah confirms him: There is no god but Allah alone with no partner; there is no god but Allah, the King, the Truth, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise; there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever utters these words in his illness, Allah forbids him to the Fire."
"6158","'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Husayn ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, that he bore witness upon Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id that they bore witness upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When the servant says: There is no god but Allah and Allah is Greatest, Allah says: My servant spoke truth; there is no god but I alone. When he says: There is no god but Allah, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, He says: My servant spoke truth; there is no god but I, and to Me belong dominion and praise. He said: And when he says: There is no god but Allah, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah, He says: He says: My servant spoke truth; there is no god but I, and there is no strength except through Me. Abu Ishaq said: Then al-Agharr said something I did not understand, so I said to Abu Ja'far: What did he say? He said: Whoever is granted them at his death, the Fire will not touch him."
"6159","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman and Abu 'Abdullah al-Agharr, the companion of Abu Hurayrah, that they heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah descends, when the last third of the night remains, to the lowest heaven every night, and says: Who complains, that I may give him; who supplicates to Me, that I may answer him; who seeks My forgiveness, that I may forgive him. That is why they used to prefer prayer at the end of the night over its beginning."
"6160","'Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Aflah ibn Humayd, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm, from Salman al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of the lone one by twenty-five degrees."
"6161","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from 'Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim people sit remembering Allah but the angels surround them, mercy covers them, and tranquility descends upon them."
"6162","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyabi narrated to us, Anas ibn 'Iyad narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, Abu 'Abdullah al-Agharr informed me, that he witnessed Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is Friday, there are angels at every door of the mosque's doors writing the first then the first; when the imam sits, they fold the scrolls and come listening to the remembrance. The likeness of the early comer is like one who offers a camel, and like one who offers a cow, and like one who offers a ram, then like one who offers a chicken, then like one who offers an egg."
"6163","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrate from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, that he bore witness upon Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id that they bore witness upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: No people sit remembering Allah but the angels surround them, mercy covers them, tranquility descends upon them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."
"6164","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, he said: I bear witness upon Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayrah that they bore witness upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No people sit remembering Allah but the angels surround them, tranquility descends upon them, mercy covers them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."
"6165","'Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh al-'Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Perform ablution from what fire has cooked."
"6166","Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Agharr ibn Muslim, also called Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: One day I entered the market with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He sat with the cloth merchants and bought trousers for four dirhams. The market people had a weigher who weighed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Weigh and give extra. The weigher said: These are words I have never heard from anyone. Abu Hurayra said: So I said to him: It is enough recklessness and harshness in your religion that you do not recognize your Prophet. He threw down the scale and rushed to the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), wanting to kiss it, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pulled his hand away from him and said: What is this? Only the non-Arabs do this with their kings, and I am not a king; I am only a man like you. So he weighed and gave extra, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the trousers. Abu Hurayra said: I went to carry it for him, and he said: The owner of a thing is most entitled to carry his own thing, unless he is weak and unable, in which case his Muslim brother helps him. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you wear trousers? He said: Yes, in travel and at home, by night and by day, for I was commanded to cover, and I found nothing more covering than them."
"6167","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard al-Agharr say: I heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, confirms His servant in five phrases he utters: when he says, there is no god but Allah with no partner, He says: My servant has spoken the truth; and when he says, there is no god but Allah and Allah is Greatest, He says: My servant has spoken the truth; and when he says, there is no god but Allah and praise be to Allah, He says: My servant has spoken the truth; and when he says, there is no god but Allah, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, He says: My servant has spoken the truth."
"6168","Abu Ishaq said: And Abu Jafar narrated to me, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayra, that he said: When he says them in his illness and then dies, he will not enter the Fire."
"6169","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad informed me, from Abu Salama, from Ibn Qariz, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."
"6170","Muhammad said: Salman al-Agharr informed me, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of this."
"6171","Abu al-Rabi al-Ataki narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid al-Madani narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Salman al-Agharr, who said: My grandfather Salman al-Agharr narrated to me: I wanted to travel for hire to Bayt al-Maqdis, and I saw Abu Hurayra, and he said: Keep to this mosque of yours, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque, and what is between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."
"6172","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am exhausted. He sent to one of his wives, and she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I have nothing but water. Then he sent to another, and she said the same, until all of them said the same: No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have nothing but water. He said: Who will host this man tonight? A man from the Ansar stood and said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He took him to his lodging and said to his wife: Do you have anything? She said: No, except the food of my children. He said: Distract them with something, and when our guest enters, light the lamp and show him that we are eating, and when he reaches out to eat, get up to the lamp and put it out. He said: They sat down and the guest ate, and in the morning he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah has wondered at what you two did tonight."
"6173","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, salt for salt, hand to hand, weight for weight; whoever gives more or takes more has dealt in usury, except where the kinds differ."
"6174","Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, his father narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three things emerge, no soul will benefit from its faith: the Beast, the Dajjal, and the rising of the sun from its setting place."
"6175","Wasil ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earth will cast out its treasures like columns of silver and gold. The thief will come and say: For this my hand was cut off. The killer will come and say: For this I killed. The one who severed kinship will come and say: For this I severed my kinship. And they will leave it, taking nothing from it."
"6176","Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurara narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from his father Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three things emerge, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith: the rising of the sun from its setting place, the emergence of the Dajjal, and the emergence of the Beast."
"6177","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: Severe exhaustion befell me, and I met Umar ibn al-Khattab and asked him to recite a verse from the Book of Allah to me. He entered his house and opened it to me. He said: I walked a short distance then fell on my face from exhaustion, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing over my head. He said: O Abu Hurayra. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and may you be made happy. He said: He took my hand and raised me up, and he recognized what was wrong with me, and took me to his lodging, and ordered a large cup of milk for me. I drank from it, then he said: Repeat, O Abu Hurayra. So I repeated and drank from it, then he said: Repeat, O Abu Hurayra. So I repeated and drank, until my belly became level and like a small cup. He said: And I saw Umar and told him about what had happened to me. He said: I said to him: One more entitled to that than you undertook it, O Umar. By Allah, I had asked you to recite the verses though I recite them better than you. Umar said: By Allah, that I had admitted you is dearer to me than red camels."
"6178","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, from Yazid, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate against the polytheists. He said: I was not sent as a curser; I was only sent as a mercy."
"6179","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never satiated his family three days in a row with wheat bread until he left this world, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"6180","Al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we mentioned Laylat al-Qadr. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of you remembers our nights at Hunayn, fair-skinned, when the moon rose like half a bowl?"
"6181","Al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: A man from the Ansar took the slaughter knife, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the Ansari's house, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of the milch animal."
"6182","Al-Harith narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Talib when death came to him: Say, there is no god but Allah; I will intercede for you on the Day of Resurrection. He said: O son of my brother, were it not that Quraysh would reproach me, I would have delighted your eye with it. Then was revealed: Indeed you do not guide whom you love."
"6183","And from Abu Hurayra, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when we heard a thud and were startled by it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is a stone that was hurled into Hell seventy autumns ago; only now has it fallen into it, and you heard it."
"6184","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gather, for I shall recite to you a third of the Quran. So they gathered, and he recited to us: Say, He is Allah, One, until he completed it, then he entered. Some of us said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said, I shall recite to you a third of the Quran, but he did not recite; this must only be due to news that came to him from heaven. He said: Then he came out to us and said: It is a third of the Quran."
"6185","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifa narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day, and there were Abu Bakr and Umar. He said: What brought you two out at this hour? They said: Hunger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I, by the One who sent me with the truth, nothing brought me out except what brought you two out. Arise. He said: They arose with him, and he came to the house of a man from the Ansar, but he was not there, only the woman. When she saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his two companions, she said: Welcome. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Where is Abu so-and-so? She said: He went to fetch us sweet water. He said: While they were so, the Ansari came with a waterskin on him. When he saw the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his two companions, he exclaimed Allah is Great, then said: Praise be to Allah, I find no people today with nobler guests. He said: He went and cut for them a bunch containing unripe and ripe dates and placed it before them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why did you not pick out? The Ansari said: O Messenger of Allah, choose with your eyes. And he took the knife and went off. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of the milch animal. He said: He slaughtered for them, and they ate from that bunch and that sheep, and drank from the water. The Prophet of Allah said to them: By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will surely be asked about this bliss on the Day of Resurrection: hunger drove you from your houses, then you did not return until you attained this; this is part of the bliss."
"6186","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifa narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, that a guest came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and he sent to his wives: Do you have anything? A guest has come to me tonight. They sent to him: No, by the One who sent you with the truth, we have nothing but water. He said: While he was so, a man from the Ansar came, and the Prophet of Allah said: Do you have anything with which to take our guest tonight? The Ansari said: Yes, O Prophet of Allah. He said: He took the guest along. When he reached his house he said to his wife: Do you have anything? She said: Yes, a loaf for us. He said: It is as if you are fixing the lamp, so put it out and set down the bread. He kept moving his hand with the guest, he and his wife, raising their hands to their mouths but eating nothing, and they left the guest alone with the bread and he ate it. In the morning the guest went off to his need. The Ansari said: The hour came when I go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he looked at me from afar and said: What did you do with your guest last night? He said: I thought the guest had complained about me to the Messenger of Allah, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I did such and such. He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and told me that your Lord wondered at what you did with your guest, or he said: laughed."
"6187","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifa narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, this nation will not perish until a man stands to a woman and lays her down in the road, and the best of them that day will be one who says: If only you hid her behind this wall."
"6188","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prompt your dying ones with there is no god but Allah."
"6189","Al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept through the two rakahs of Fajr and prayed them after the sun had risen."
"6190","Abu Mamar Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, that a man married a woman from the Ansar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Did you not look at her? For there is something in the eyes of the Ansar. He said: I have looked."
"6191","Hashim ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man outbidding his brother, forbade najsh, forbade meeting the caravans, forbade a woman asking for the divorce of her sister, forbade withholding water lest the herbage be grazed, and forbade a townsman selling for a bedouin. Whoever grants a milch animal as a gift, its morning milk and evening milk come and go as charity."
"6192","Hashim narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever walks with a funeral until it is finished has two qirats, and whoever returns before it is finished has one qirat. We said: What is the qirat, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Like Uhud."
"6193","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Hamza al-Zayyat, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah said: Remember Me within yourself and I shall remember you within Myself, and remember Me in an assembly of people and I shall remember you in an assembly, meaning better than them."
"6194","Suwayd ibn Said and others narrated to us, they said: Marwan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam began as a stranger and will return as a stranger as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers."
"6195","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Abdullah, freedman of Banu Umayya, from Abu Hazim and Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I owe the Hajj of Islam and I owe a debt. He said: Then pay your debt."
"6196","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yunus, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant seeks refuge from the Fire seven times in a day except that the Fire says: O Lord, Your servant so-and-so has sought refuge in You from me, so grant him refuge. And no servant asks Allah for Paradise seven times in a day except that Paradise says: O Lord, Your servant so-and-so asked me, so admit him."
"6197","Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiya narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I sought my Lord's permission to seek forgiveness for my mother and He did not permit me, and I sought His permission to visit her grave and He permitted me."
"6198","Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Abu Hurayra, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, exhaustion has befallen me. He sent to his wives and found nothing with them. He said: Is there no man to host this one tonight? A man stood and went to his family, and said to his family: The guest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); do not withhold anything from him. She said: By Allah, I have nothing but the food of the children. He said: When the children want dinner, put them to sleep, and come and put out the lamp, and we shall fold our stomachs tonight. She did so. Then the man went in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah has wondered - or: Allah has laughed - at so-and-so and so-and-so. And Allah revealed: And they prefer others over themselves though they be in need."
"6199","Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, Ziyad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no tree in Paradise except that its trunk is of gold."
"6200","Abu Mamar narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man calls his wife to his bed and she does not answer him, and she sleeps disobedient, the angels curse her until morning."
"6201","Abu Mamar narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whom Allah will not speak to nor look at on the Day of Resurrection, and theirs is a painful punishment: a lying ruler, a poor arrogant one, and an old adulterer."
"6202","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs Hajj to the House without obscenity or sin returns as on the day his mother bore him."
"6203","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra - it was said to Sufyan: Did he raise it? He said: Perhaps - : Charity is not lawful for a rich man, nor for one possessing sound strength."
"6204","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is guarded from the evil of what is between his jaws and between his legs will enter Paradise."
"6205","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim al-Ashjai, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever purifies himself in his house then walks to a house from the houses of Allah to fulfill an obligation from the obligations of Allah, his two steps are: one erases a sin and the other raises a rank."
"6206","Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Sad ibn Tariq, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adornment of Paradise reaches where ablution reaches. That is because Abu Hurayra once performed ablution and the ablution reached his armpits."
"6207","Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Sad ibn Tariq, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Hour will not come until Allah sends a red wind from the direction of Yemen, and Allah will gather every soul that believes in Allah and the Last Day. And what people remark about the few who die from it: the elder of so-and-so's tribe has died, the old woman of so-and-so's tribe has died!"
"6208","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, from Sad ibn Tariq, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: This nation is a nation shown mercy; there is no punishment upon it except what it inflicts upon itself. He said: I said: How does it punish itself? He said: Was not the Day of al-Nahr a punishment? Was not the Day of the Camel a punishment? Was not the Day of Siffin a punishment?"
"6209","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Zaida, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The quickest Arab tribes to perish are Quraysh, and soon a passerby will pass a sandal and say: This is the sandal of a Qurashi."
"6210","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra - he said: I think he raised it - he said: There is no negligence in tasbih or prayer."
"6211","Huraym ibn Abd al-Ala ibn al-Furat al-Asadi and Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, they said: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: Abu Jahl said: Does Muhammad soil his face among you? They said: Yes. He said: By that by which we swear, if I saw that I would surely tread on his neck. He said: It was said to him: There he is praying, so he came to him, claiming he would tread on his neck. He said: Nothing startled him from him except that he was recoiling on his heels and shielding himself with his hands. His companions reached him and said: What is wrong with you, O Abu al-Hakam? He said: Between me and him there is a trench of fire and wings. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, if he had come near me the angels would have snatched him limb by limb. He said: Then Allah revealed: Have you seen the one who forbids a servant when he prays, Have you seen if he denies and turns away - meaning Abu Jahl - Does he not know that Allah sees, to the end of the verses, So let him call his assembly - his people - We shall call the guards - he said: the angels - No, do not obey him, and He commanded him with what He commanded him with. Huraym said: al-Mutamir said: My father said this - whether he mentioned it from Abu Hurayra or not - when he mentioned: Have you seen the one who forbids a servant when he prays."
"6212","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abu Ismail, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: We camped for the night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and we did not wake until the sun hurt us. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let each man take hold of his mount's head, then move away from these dwellings. Then he called for water and performed ablution, prayed two rakahs, then the prayer was established."
"6213","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will come radiant with white marks from ablution, a mark of my nation that belongs to no one else."
"6214","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ubayda narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog and the dowry of a prostitute."
"6215","Abu Bakr and Uthman narrated to us, they said: Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Furat, from his father, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Children of Israel were governed by their prophets; whenever a prophet went, a prophet succeeded him, and there will be none among you - meaning a prophet. They said: What will there be, O Messenger of Allah? He said: There will be caliphs, and many. They said: What shall we do? He said: Fulfill the pledge to the first, then the first, and render what is upon you, and Allah will ask them about what is upon them. And in Uthman's hadith: The prophets govern them."
"6216","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whom Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify, nor look at, and theirs is a painful punishment: a lying king, a poor arrogant one, and an old adulterer."
"6217","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man calls his wife to his bed and she does not come to him, and he sleeps angry with her, the angels curse her until morning."
"6218","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never faulted food at all; when he desired it he ate it, and when he disliked it he left it."
"6219","Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Salim ibn Abi Hafsa narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves al-Hasan and al-Husayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me."
"6220","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, and from Ribi, from Hudhayfa, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah let those before us stray from Friday; the Jews had Saturday and the Christians had Sunday, then Allah brought us and guided us to Friday, and made Friday, Saturday and Sunday. Likewise they follow us on the Day of Resurrection: we are the last in this world, the first on the Day of Resurrection, those judged for on the Day of Resurrection before creation. Allah will gather people on one plain, and the believers will say when Paradise is brought near: Who will open Paradise for us? They will come to Adam and say: O Adam, open Paradise for us. He will say: Did anything expel you from Paradise except the sin of your father Adam? I am not the one for that; go to your father Ibrahim, the close friend of his Lord. They will come to him and say: O Ibrahim, open Paradise for us. He will say: I am not the one for that; I was only a close friend from afar. Go to my brother Musa, to whom Allah spoke directly. They will come to Musa, and he will say: I am not the one for that; go to Allah's word and spirit, Isa. They will come to him, and he will say: I am not the one for that; go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They will come to Muhammad, and he will seek permission and it will be granted to him, and trust and kinship will be sent with him and will stand on the two sides of the Sirat, right and left. The first of you will pass like lightning - how it passes - then return in a blink, then pass like the wind, then pass like a bird, then like the running of men, their deeds carrying them along. Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will be standing on the Sirat saying: Grant safety. Until people's deeds fail them, until a man will come unable to pass except crawling. On the edges of the Sirat are suspended hooks, commanded, seizing whom they are commanded to seize: one saved but scratched, and one piled into the Fire. By the One in whose hand is Abu Hurayra's soul, the depth of Hell is ninety autumns."
"6221","Shuja ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Abi Ali, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the commanders, woe to the headmen, woe to the trustees. Peoples will wish on the Day of Resurrection that their forelocks had been tied to the Pleiades, dangling between heaven and earth, and that they had never undertaken any office."
"6222","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaida, from Maysara al-Ashjai, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest's due. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the guest's due? He said: Three days, and what is beyond that is charity. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him witness to good or be silent. And treat women well, for woman was created from a rib, and the most crooked part of the rib is its top; if you set it straight you will break it, and if you leave it it will remain crooked. And treat women well."
"6223","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abdullah ibn Jumay, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of poor memory. He said: Open your cloak. He said: I opened it. He said: Gather it. He said: I never forgot anything after that."
"6224","Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us, Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Rafi, from Abu Abdullah the cousin of Abu Hurayra, from Abu Hurayra, who said: People have abandoned Amin. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he recited: Not of those who earned anger nor of those astray, would say Amin until he made the first row hear."
"6225","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Rafi, from Abu Abdullah the cousin of Abu Hurayra, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman would begin the recitation with: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"6226","Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Qazaa ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says there is no god but Allah with certainty will enter Paradise."
"6227","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Qazaa narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Salama ibn Junada, from Hanash, from Abu Hurayra, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came bringing a fat, choice yearling goat and a lean, worthless yearling sheep. He said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a lean, worthless yearling sheep, and this is a fat, choice yearling goat, the better of the two; shall I sacrifice it? He said: Sacrifice it, for to Allah belongs the good."
"6228","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Ziyad, from al-Hasan, who said: I heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites Ya Sin in a night wakes forgiven, and whoever recites Ha Mim in which Dukhan is mentioned on Friday night wakes forgiven."
"6229","Shayban narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: Abu Hurayra met a man in Madina and said to him: It is as if you are not from this town. He said: Yes. He said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Allah may benefit you by it? He said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first thing the son of Adam will be reckoned for is his prayer. Allah says to His angels: Look into My servant's prayer; if they find it complete it is written for him as complete, and if they find it lacking anything, He says: See if you find any voluntary prayer for him. He said: His prayer is completed from his voluntary prayers, and the deeds are taken in like measure."
"6230","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abu Hurayra, who said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three things I shall never abandon: witr before sleep, fasting three days of every month, and ghusl on Friday."
"6231","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When he sits between her four parts then exerts effort, ghusl becomes obligatory upon them both, even if he does not ejaculate."
"6232","Wahb ibn Baqiyya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from a man of Banu Sulayt, who said: I was in an estate of mine and saw a crowd. I said: What is this? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is admonishing his companions. I put my head between the people, and there was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim - three times - he does not wrong him nor abandon him. Piety is here, and he pointed with his hand to his chest."
"6233","Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will take from what Allah and His Messenger have made obligatory a word or two, or three, or four, or five, gather them in the edge of his garment and learn them? He said: I spread my garment while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was speaking, then I gathered it, and I hope I have not forgotten any hadith from what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said."
"6234","Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Umayya Abd al-Karim, who said: al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan narrated, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept prayer except with purification, nor charity from misappropriated spoils."
"6235","Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: Abu Hurayra narrated to us, while we were then in Madina, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deeds will be presented on the Day of Resurrection. Prayer will come and say: O Lord, I am prayer. Allah, mighty and exalted, will say: You are upon good. Then charity will come and say: O Lord, I am charity. He will say: You are upon good. Fasting will come and the deeds will come likewise, saying: O Lord. And there will come - I think he said: Islam - and it will say: O Lord, You are Peace and I am Islam. Allah will say: You are upon good; by you I take today and by you I give. Then al-Hasan said: Indeed the religion with Allah is Islam, and whoever seeks other than Islam as religion, it will never be accepted from him, and he is among the losers in the Hereafter."
"6236","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abu al-Muqaddam narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever recites Surat al-Dukhan on Friday night wakes forgiven."
"6237","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah and Zakariya ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Hushaym narrated to us, Abbad ibn Rashid al-Minqari informed us, he said: I heard Said ibn Abi Khayra narrating from al-Hasan; al-Hasan informed me, some forty years ago, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon people a time when they consume usury. He said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, all of them? He said: Whoever of them does not consume it will be touched by its dust."
"6238","Zakariya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the rider greet the walker, the walker the seated, and the few the many."
"6239","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may utter a word, not thinking it will reach where it reached, by which he falls into the Fire seventy autumns."
"6240","Shayban narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, who said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things, the hadith."
"6241","Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Women who seek divorce without cause and who strip themselves are the hypocrites."
"6242","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Mughira ibn Muslim, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah loves leniency in selling, leniency in buying, leniency in settling."
"6243","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"6244","Ishaq narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Tariq al-Sadi narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will take from me these words and act upon them or teach them to one who will act upon them? He said: I said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He took my hand and counted five therein and said: Guard against prohibitions and you will be the most worshipful of people; be content with what Allah has apportioned for you and you will be the richest of people; do good to your neighbor and you will be a believer; love for people what you love for yourself and you will be a Muslim; and do not laugh much, for much laughter deadens the heart."
"6245","Zakariya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Kathir, he said: I heard Said ibn Abi Khayra narrating to Dawud ibn Abi Hind; al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon people a time when they consume usury. They said: All people - or: all the people? He said: Whoever does not consume it will be touched by its dust."
"6246","Abu Ubayd from Abu Hurayra. Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd, freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: That one of you gather a bundle of firewood, carry it on his back and sell it, is better for him than asking a man who then gives him or withholds from him."
"6247","Al-Hasan ibn Ismail, a Basran, narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd, freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one whom his deed will admit into Paradise. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me with mercy from Him."
"6248","Tawus from Abu Hurayra. Al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayra, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and once he mentioned it without raising it - that Sulayman, peace be upon him, swore an oath that he would go round ninety women tonight, each bearing a boy who would fight in the path of Allah. The angel - or his companion - said: Say, if Allah wills. He forgot, and went round them, and no woman brought anything except one of them, who brought half a boy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had Sulayman made the exception, he would not have broken his oath, and it would have been attainment for him in his need."
"6249","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, who heard Tawus say: I heard Abu Hurayra narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Adam and Musa argued. Musa said: O Adam, you are our father, and you expelled us from Paradise by your sin. Adam said to him: O Musa, Allah chose you and wrote the Torah for you with His hand; why do you blame me for a matter Allah decreed for me forty years before He created me? So Adam overcame Musa."
"6250","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil and Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears and says, if Allah wills, has not broken his oath."
"6251","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayra, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): People will be resurrected upon their intentions."
"6252","Al-Araj from Abu Hurayra. Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, saying: You claim that Abu Hurayra narrates much from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah is the appointor. I was a poor man serving the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for my bellyful, while the Muhajirun were occupied with trading in the markets, and the Ansar were occupied tending their properties. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spreads his garment and will not forget anything he hears from me. So I spread my garment until he finished his hadith, then I gathered it to me, and I never forgot anything I heard from him."
"6253","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you has a neighbor ask permission to fix a timber in his wall, let him not forbid him."
"6254","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra: The worst food is the food of the wedding feast, to which the rich are invited and the poor left out. Whoever does not come to the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"6255","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Rabia ibn Uthman, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The strong believer is better and dearer to Allah than the weak believer, and each is upon good. Strive for what benefits you, seek Allah's help and do not despair. If something befalls you, do not say: Had I done such and such; but say: Allah decreed and what He willed He did, for if opens the work of Satan."
"6256","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The crescent was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: When you see it, fast, and when you see it, break fast; if it is obscured to you, count thirty."
"6257","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Ayyub; Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is offered sweet basil, let him not refuse it, for it is light to carry and sweet in scent."
"6258","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Ayyub, he said: Jafar ibn Rabia informed me, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you hear the crowing of roosters, they have seen an angel, so ask and supplicate. When you hear the braying of a donkey, it has seen a devil, so seek refuge in Allah from the evil of what it saw."
"6259","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you performs ablution, let him put water in his nose then blow it out."
"6260","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Surplus water is not to be withheld so as to withhold herbage thereby."
"6261","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, conveying to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The old man remains youthful in love of two things: love of life and love of wealth."
"6262","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is not from abundance of goods; richness is richness of soul."
"6263","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, conveying to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: O son of Adam, spend and I shall spend upon you. And he said: Allah's right hand is full, overflowing, nothing diminishes it, night and day."
"6264","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, conveying to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you looks at one favored over him in wealth and body, let him look at one below him in wealth and body."
"6265","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall pray in a single garment with nothing of it upon his shoulder."
"6266","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No one is wounded in the path of Allah - and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path - except that he will come on the Day of Resurrection with his wound flowing blood; the color that of blood, the scent that of musk."
"6267","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, conveying to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: People follow Quraysh in this matter; their Muslims follow their Muslims, and their disbelievers follow their disbelievers."
"6268","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You will find among the worst of people the two-faced one, who comes to these with one face and to those with another."
"6269","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra - as a narration - : When one of you wakes fasting, let him not utter obscenity nor act ignorantly; if a man reviles him or fights him, let him say: I am fasting, I am fasting."
"6270","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra - as a narration - he said: Do not meet the caravans for purchase, nor tie up the udders of camels and sheep. Whoever buys them after that has the better of the two choices: if he wishes he may keep it, and if he wishes he may return it with a sa of dates, not wheat. Abu Khaythama said: Meaning wheat."
"6271","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, conveying: Is there no man who grants a she-camel to a household, its evening and morning milk coming and going? Its reward is immense. Abu Khaythama said: Had he said with large cups, it would have been better."
"6272","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: We are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, except that every nation..."
"6273","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would command them to delay Isha, and I would command them to use the siwak at every prayer."
"6274","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, conveying, he said: The Hour will come while a man is milking the milch camel, and the vessel will not reach his mouth before it comes; and two men trading a garment, they will not complete the trade before it comes; and a man plastering his basin, he will not draw from it before it comes."
"6275","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me."
"6276","And with its chain from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A woman shall not fast a day besides Ramadan while her husband is present except with his permission."
"6277","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, conveying, he said: When one of you strikes, let him avoid the face."
"6278","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, conveying, he said: The food of two suffices three, and the food of three suffices four."
"6279","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah said: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and what has never occurred to a human heart. Its Confirmation in Allah's Book: No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort of eyes as reward for what they used to do."
"6280","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, as a narration, he said: Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred minus one; whoever preserves them will enter Paradise. And He is Odd, loving the odd."
"6281","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Satan ties three knots upon the nape of one of you; when he wakes and remembers Allah, one knot is loosened; when he performs ablution, two knots are loosened; when he prays, the knots are loosened; otherwise he wakes evil in soul, lazy."
"6282","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave, seek refuge in Allah from the trial of the False Messiah, the Dajjal, seek refuge in Allah from the trial of life and death."
"6283","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you is invited to food while fasting, let him say: I am fasting."
"6284","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah said: My mercy has preceded My wrath."
"6285","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah said: If My servant intends a good deed, write it for him as a good deed; if he does it, write it tenfold; if he intends an evil deed, do not write it; if he does it, write it as one evil; if he leaves it, write it as a good deed."
"6286","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay by the rich is injustice, and when one of you is referred to one who can pay, let him follow."
"6287","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever catches a prostration of Asr prayer, and of Fajr prayer, before the sun rises or before it sets, has caught the prayer."
"6288","Bishr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Surplus water is not to be withheld so as to withhold herbage thereby."
"6289","Bishr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best day upon which the sun has risen is Friday; in it Adam was created, in it he was expelled from Paradise, and in it he was returned to it."
"6290","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided with awe, and given the concise speech. While I was sleeping I was brought the keys of the earth's treasuries and placed in my hand."
"6291","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Excellent charity is a choice milch camel given as a gift, or a choice ewe whose morning vessel and evening vessel come."
"6292","Bishr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a woman was nursing her son, a rider passed by her as she nursed him. She said: O Allah, do not cause my son to die until he becomes like this rider. He said: O Allah, do not make me like him. Then he returned to the breast. Then a woman was passed by, being dragged while children played with her. She said: O Allah, do not make my son like her. He said: O Allah, make me like her. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: As for the rider, he is a disbeliever. As for the woman, they say to her: You commit adultery, and she says: Allah suffices me. They say to her: You steal, and she says: Allah suffices me."
"6293","Bishr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Paradise and Hell disputed. Hell said: I have been favored with the arrogant and tyrants. Paradise said: Why does none enter me except the weak, the lowly and the helpless among people? Allah said to Paradise: You are only My mercy, I show mercy through you to whom I will. And He said to Hell: You are only My punishment, I punish through you whom I will. And each of you shall have its fill."
"6294","Bishr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earth consumes every son of Adam except the tailbone; from it he was created and in it he will be recomposed."
"6295","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Mashar al-Madani narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will surely follow as the nations before you followed, cubit by cubit, span by span, fathom by fathom, until if one of them entered a lizard's hole you would enter it. Abu Hurayra said: Recite if you wish the Quran: Like those before you, mightier than you in strength, to the end of the verse. They said: O Messenger of Allah, as Persia and Rome did? He said: Who are people but they?"
"6296","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Mashar al-Madani narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi and Musa ibn Sad, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until harj increases. They said: What is harj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Killing. Three times. They said: Every year we kill a thousand or two thousand of the polytheists? He said: I do not mean that, but some of you will kill others. They said: While we are alive and do that? He said: Allah will deaden the hearts of the people of that time as He deadens their bodies."
"6297","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the believer is like the tender plant of crops; winds bend it until a wind comes to it and lays it down."
"6298","Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, Halbas ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have married off my daughter and I would like you to help me with something. He said: I have nothing, but tomorrow bring me a wide-mouthed flask and a tree branch... and he mentioned the hadith in al-Fawaid."
"6299","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abu Said narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Sulayman, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear the braying of a donkey, the barking of a dog, and the voice of a rooster at night, seek refuge in Allah from Satan, for they see what you do not see."
"6300","Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Jafar ibn Rabia narrated to him that Abd al-Rahman al-Araj narrated to him from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No hama, no hama."
"6301","Suwayd narrated to us, from Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay by the rich is injustice, and if one of you is referred to one who can pay, let him follow."
"6302","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Uqba narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer."
"6303","Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The thief does not steal while he is a believer, nor drink wine when he drinks while he is a believer, nor commit adultery while he is a believer."
"6304","Abu al-Zinad said: And Abu Salama narrated to me, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nor does he plunder a plunder to which Muslims raise their heads while he is a believer."
"6305","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rakah of Fajr before sunrise has caught Fajr, or two rakahs of Asr before sunset has caught Asr."
"6306","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you remains in prayer so long as prayer detains him, and nothing prevents him returning to his family except waiting for prayer."
"6307","Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A prophet among the prophets lodged under a tree, and an ant bit him. He ordered his baggage removed from beneath it, then ordered it burned. It was revealed to him: Was it not a single ant?"
"6308","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me as I have left you; those before you perished only by their questioning and differing over their prophets. What I forbid you, avoid it; what I command you, do of it what you can."
"6309","Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every newborn is born upon fitra; his parents make him a Jew or a Christian, as camels produce from a sound beast - do you sense any mutilated? They said: What of one who dies, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"6310","And from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Woe to you, ride it."
"6311","Abu al-Qasim Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami said: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Hamdun al-Sulami informed us, Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdun al-Hiri informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Tamimi al-Mawsili informed us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The injury caused by a stray animal is of no liability, mines are of no liability, wells are of no liability, and one-fifth is due on buried treasure."
"6312","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you asks his brother to place a wooden beam on his wall, let him do so."
"6313","Wahb narrated to us with the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah: The Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, divide the wealth between us and our brothers among the Muhajirun. He said: You will not be spared the burden of maintenance, but share the fruits with them. They said: We hear and obey."
"6314","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fights, let him avoid the face."
"6315","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, there is no believing man or woman on the face of the earth except that I am closer to him than himself; whichever of you leaves a debt or dependents, let it be referred to me, for I am his guardian, and whichever of you leaves wealth, it belongs to his heirs."
"6316","With the same chain, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I take a covenant with You that You will never break: I am only a human being, so whichever of the believers I strike, revile, harm, or curse, make it mercy, purification, and nearness for him by which You draw him near on the Day of Resurrection."
"6317","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay the prayer until it cools, for the intensity of heat is from the blast of Hell."
"6318","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: Al-karm (the vine); al-karm is only the Muslim man."
"6319","With the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The space of a whip of one of you in Paradise is better than what is between heaven and earth."
"6320","With the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you outbid his brother, nor propose marriage over his brother's proposal until he marries or leaves."
"6321","With the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the Hijrah I would have been a man of the Ansar; if people took a valley or a path and the Ansar took a valley or a path, I would take the valley of the Ansar or the path of the Ansar."
"6322","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hoarded wealth of one of you on the Day of Resurrection will be a bald-headed venomous snake; its owner will flee from it and it will pursue him, saying: I am your treasure, until it puts his finger in its mouth."
"6323","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant of one of you brings his food, having borne its heat and preparation for him, let him say: Sit and eat, or let him take some of the food for him; and he gestured with his hand, meaning like this and like this, let him place it in his palm and say: Eat all of these."
"6324","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet the riders for trade, do not engage in najsh (false bidding), let none of you sell over another's sale, and do not tie up the udders of camels and sheep; whoever buys them after that has the better of the two options after milking them: if he is pleased he keeps it, and if he dislikes it he returns it along with a sa' of dates."
"6325","With the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until one of you increases wealth and it overflows, until the owner of wealth is concerned about who will accept it from him, and until he offers it and the one to whom he offers it says: I have no need of it."
"6326","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until knowledge is taken away, ignorance increases, trials appear, time draws near, and al-harj increases. They said: What is al-harj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Killing, killing."
"6327","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at the one who drags his lower garment or his cloak out of arrogance."
"6328","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Imam is only a shield; fighting is done behind him and protection is sought through him. If he commands fear of Allah and justice, he has reward for that, and if he commands otherwise, he bears part of it."
"6329","With the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Imam is appointed only to be followed, so do not differ from him: when he says Allahu Akbar, say Allahu Akbar; when he bows, bow; when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: Our Lord, to You belongs praise; when he prostrates, prostrate; and when he prays sitting, pray seated all together."
"6330","With the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O sons of Abd Manaf, ransom yourselves from Allah; O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, ransom yourselves from Allah; O Umm al-Zubayr, aunt of Muhammad; O Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, I own nothing for you from Allah; ransom yourselves from Allah; ask me of my wealth whatever you wish."
"6331","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number."
"6332","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ghifar, may Allah forgive her, and Aslam, may Allah grant her safety."
"6333","With the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Angels succeed one another among you, angels of the night and angels of the day; then they gather at the Asr prayer and the Fajr prayer, then those who spent the night among you ascend and He asks them, though He knows best: How did you leave My servants? They say: We came to them while they were praying and left them while they were praying."
"6334","With the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leads people in prayer, let him lighten it, for among them are the sick, the weak, and the one with needs; and when one of you prays alone, let him lengthen as he wishes."
"6335","Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rak'ah of the Asr prayer before the sun sets, or of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises, has caught the prayer."
"6336","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan ties three knots on the back of the head of one of you, striking upon each knot: You have a long night, so sleep. If he wakes and remembers his Lord, one knot is loosened; if he performs ablution, a knot is loosened; if he prays, a knot is loosened, and he wakes energetic and good-spirited; if he does not, he wakes evil-spirited and lazy."
"6337","With the same chain, he said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty will not look on the Day of Resurrection at a man who drags his lower garment out of arrogance. He said: While a man was strutting in his two garments, admiring himself, Allah caused the earth to swallow him, and he keeps sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection."
"6338","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you see my qiblah here? By Allah, your humility and your bowing are not hidden from me; I see you from behind my back."
"6339","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say al-karm; al-karm is only the Muslim man."
"6340","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor person is not this roaming beggar whom people turn away with a morsel, a date, or two dates. They said: Who is the poor person, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The one who finds no sufficiency to enrich him, is not noticed so charity is given to him, and does not stand to ask people."
"6341","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I intended to order firewood to be gathered, then order the prayer to be announced, then order a man to lead the people, then go to men and burn their houses over them. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if one of them knew he would find a fat bone or two good trotters, he would attend the Isha prayer."
"6342","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty said: When the servant loves meeting Me, I love meeting him, and when he dislikes meeting Me, I dislike meeting him."
"6343","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The head of disbelief is toward the east; pride and arrogance are among the owners of horses, camels, and the loud-voiced farmers, and tranquility is among the owners of sheep."
"6344","With the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Imam is only a shield; fighting is done behind him. If he is God-fearing and just, he has reward for that; if he commands otherwise, he bears part of it. The Imam is appointed only to be followed."
"6345","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Angels succeed one another among you, angels by night and angels by day, and they gather at the Asr prayer and the Fajr prayer; then those who spent the night among you ascend to Him, and He asks them, though He knows best: How did you leave My servants? They say: We left them while they were praying and came to them while they were praying."
"6346","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwak."
"6347","He said: The Right Hand of Allah is full; expenditure does not diminish it, flowing by night and by day. Have you seen what He has spent since He created the heavens and the earth? It has not diminished what is in His Right Hand; His Throne is upon the water, and in His other Hand is the Balance, lowering and raising."
"6348","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delaying payment by the rich is injustice; when one of you is referred to a solvent man, let him accept the transfer."
"6349","With the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet the riders for trade, let none of you sell over another's sale, do not engage in najsh, let no town-dweller sell for a bedouin, and do not tie up the udders of camels or sheep; whoever buys them after that has the better of the two options after milking: if pleased he keeps it, and if displeased he returns it along with a sa' of dates."
"6350","Khalid ibn Mirdas Abu al-Haytham narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Rabi'ah, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The strong believer is better, more excellent, and more beloved to Allah than the weak believer, though in each there is good. Strive for what benefits you and do not despair; if something overcomes you, say: Allah decreed and did what He willed. Beware of 'if only', for 'if only' opens the work of Satan."
"6351","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah; and from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, one of them as narration, he said: Sulayman (peace be upon him) said: I will go to a hundred women tonight, each bearing a boy who will fight in the path of Allah. The angel said to him: Say: If Allah wills. He forgot, and went to them, and none bore except one woman who bore half a boy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if he had said: If Allah wills, each of them would have borne a boy fighting in the path of Allah, and it would have fulfilled his need."
"6352","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Yazid ibn Iyad ibn Ju'dubah narrated to us, al-A'raj narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not like a Muslim to spend the night in a state of janabah; I fear he may die and the angels will not attend his funeral."
"6353","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan informed me, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our dwelling tomorrow, if Allah wills, is at al-Khayf, the mosque of Banu Kinanah, where they swore upon disbelief."
"6354","Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Abu Maryam, from Abu Hurayrah, that he heard him say: Whoever sees his brother, let him greet him with peace; if a tree, wall, or rock comes between them and then he meets him, let him greet him."
"6355","With the same chain, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"6356","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever narrates a narration and someone sneezes at it, it is true."
"6357","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no man pray in a single garment with nothing of it upon his shoulder."
"6358","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, he said: Amr informed me, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon an old man walking between his two sons, leaning on them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter with this old man? His two sons said: O Messenger of Allah, he had a vow upon him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ride, O old man, for Allah Almighty is free of need of you and your vow."
"6359","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Amr informed me, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A vow does not bring the son of Adam anything Allah has not decreed; rather the vow coincides with the decree, and thereby is extracted from the miser what the miser did not intend to give."
"6360","Ibrahim ibn Ar'arah narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hashimi narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril (peace be upon him) commanded me with sincere counsel."
"6361","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Jamil ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sets out for Hajj and dies, Allah writes for him the reward of the pilgrim until the Day of Resurrection; whoever sets out for Umrah and dies, Allah writes for him the reward of the one performing Umrah until the Day of Resurrection; and whoever sets out as a warrior in the path of Allah and dies, Allah writes for him the reward of the warrior until the Day of Resurrection."
"6362","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you enter upon your Muslim brother, eat of his food without asking him, and drink of his drink without asking him."
"6363","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Ata ibn Yazid, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever glorifies Allah thirty-three times, magnifies Him thirty-three times, and praises Him thirty-three times, and says: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and praise, and He is over all things Powerful, after the prayer, his sins are forgiven even if they are more than the foam of the sea."
"6364","Al-Hasan ibn Ismail Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: People said: O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you suffer harm in seeing the sun with no clouds below it, or the moon on the night of full moon? They said: No. He said: Likewise you will see Him. Allah will gather people on the Day of Resurrection and say: Whoever worshipped something, let him follow it. So whoever worshipped the sun will follow the sun, whoever worshipped the moon will follow the moon, and whoever worshipped idols will follow idols, until this Ummah remains with its intercessors, and the bridge is laid across Hell. Then I will be called and be the first to speak, and none will speak that day except the Messengers, whose plea that day is: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. Upon the bridge are hooks like the thorns of al-sa'dan. Have you seen al-sa'dan? They said: Yes. He said: They are like its thorns, except none knows their enormity but Allah Almighty; they snatch people according to their deeds. Among them is the believer saved by his deeds, and among them the requited one. When Allah finishes judging between the servants, He orders the angels to bring out of the Fire whoever did not associate anything with Allah, among those Allah wills to mercy; they bring them out, recognizing them by the marks of prostration, for Allah Almighty forbade the Fire to consume the marks of prostration. Water of life is poured over them and they grow as seeds grow in flood-borne soil. One man remains facing the Fire, saying: My Lord, turn my face away; its wind has struck me and its smoke burned me. He says: If I grant you that, will you ask Me for anything else? He says: No, by Your Might. He gives Allah whatever covenants He wills, and keeps praying until his face is turned from the Fire. When he faces Paradise he is silent as long as Allah wills, then says: My Lord, bring me to the gate of Paradise. Allah Almighty says: Woe to you, son of Adam, how treacherous you are; did you not give Me your covenants not to ask for other than what I gave you? He keeps praying until He says: Perhaps if I grant you that you will ask Me for more? He gives his Lord whatever covenants He wills not to ask for more, and He brings him to the gate of Paradise. When he stands at its gate, Paradise bursts open for him and he sees its bliss and joy; he is silent as long as Allah wills, then says: My Lord, admit me to Paradise. He says: Son of Adam, how treacherous you are; did you not give Me your covenants not to ask for other than what I gave you? He says: My Lord, let me not be the most wretched of Your creation; he keeps praying and asking until he is told: Enter Paradise. It is said to him: Wish. He wishes until Allah reminds him of this and that, until his wishes end, and He says: This is yours and its like with it. Ata ibn Yazid said: Abu Sa'id was with Abu Hurayrah hearing his narration without rejecting anything, until when he said: This is yours and its like with it, Abu Sa'id said: This is yours and ten times its like. Abu Hurayrah said: I remembered only: This is yours and its like with it. Abu Sa'id said: I bear witness that I remembered from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: It is yours and ten times its like. Abu Hurayrah said: That is the last man to enter Paradise."
"6365","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Suhayl, from Abu Ubayd, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever glorifies Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, praises thirty-three times, and magnifies thirty-three times, that is ninety-nine, and says to complete one hundred: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and praise, and He is over all things Powerful, his sins are forgiven even if they are like the foam of the sea."
"6366","Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad informed us, Mu'ammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the bridge are the thorns of sa'dan; have you seen al-sa'dan?"
"6367","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits it, the thief does not steal while he is a believer when he steals, and he does not drink wine while he is a believer when he drinks it. In Ata's narration: Nor does he plunder a valuable prize while he is a believer. He said: Faith is stripped from him; if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance."
"6368","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Dawud al-Attar narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"6369","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take suhur, for in suhur there is blessing."
"6370","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked blessing upon suhur and tharid."
"6371","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Layth, from Ata and Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am ruined. He said: What is that? He said: I approached my wife in Ramadan. He said: Free a slave. He said: I cannot find one. He said: Offer a camel. He said: I cannot find one. He said: Sit. A man gave him something, and he said: Give this in charity, for it suffices for you. He said: None is needier of it, O Messenger of Allah, than my dependents. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought nineteen or twenty or twenty-one sa's, and he gave them to him, saying: For you and your dependents."
"6372","Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qays ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three things: witr before sleep, fasting three days of every month, and the two rak'ahs of Duha."
"6373","Al-Hasan ibn Shabib al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you performs ablution, let him rinse his mouth and sniff water into his nose; and the ears are part of the head."
"6374","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the hire of a stallion for mating."
"6375","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah has one hundred mercies; He sent down one among mankind, jinn, beasts, and vermin, by which they show affection and mercy, and by which wild beasts are tender to their young; and He kept ninety-nine mercies for Himself, by which He will mercy His servants on the Day of Resurrection."
"6376","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever learns knowledge seeking thereby the Face of Allah, yet learns it only to attain worldly gain, will not find the fragrance of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection."
"6377","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr informed me that Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to him that Sa'id ibn Yasar narrated to him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to a town that consumes towns: Yathrib, which is Madinah; it expels people as the bellows expels the dross of iron."
"6378","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Tamim, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dinar for dinar with no excess between them."
"6379","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, he said: Musa ibn Abi Tamim narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dinar for dinar, and dirham for dirham, with no excess between them."
"6380","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah created Adam, He wiped his back, and every soul to exist until the Day of Resurrection fell from his back; He presented them to Adam, who saw in each man's face a glimmer of light, and saw one man whose glimmer pleased him. He said: Who is this, my Lord? He said: This is one of your offspring named Dawud. He said: How long is his life, my Lord? He said: Sixty years. He said: Add forty years of my life to him. He said: Then it is written, sealed, and not changed. When Adam's life ran out except the forty he had granted Dawud, the Angel of Death came to him. Adam said: Forty years of my life remain. He said: Did you not give them to your son Dawud? He said: He denied, so his offspring denied; Adam erred, so his offspring erred; he forgot, so his offspring forgot. He saw among them the strong and the weak, the rich and the poor, and the afflicted. He said: My Lord, why did You not make them equal? He said: I wanted to be thanked."
"6381","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, freedman of Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor person is not the one turned away by one date or two, or one morsel or two; the poor person is only the abstinent one. Recite if you wish: They do not ask people importunately."
"6382","Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one."
"6383","Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one."
"6384","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ata ibn Mina, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: We prostrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at: When the sky is rent asunder, and: Read in the name of your Lord who created."
"6385","Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to prostrate at: Read in the name of your Lord, and: When the sky is rent asunder."
"6386","Shayban narrated to us, Umarah ibn Zadham al-Saydalani narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no man who memorizes knowledge and is asked about it but conceals it, except he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."
"6387","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Hani al-Khawlani Humayd ibn Hani narrated to us, from Abu Uthman Muslim ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the end of time there will be people of my Ummah who narrate to you what neither you nor your fathers heard; beware of them."
"6388","Abu Abdullah Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah: A woman passed with her perfume diffusing, and he said: O maidservant of the Almighty, do you intend the mosque? She said: Yes. He said: Did you perfume yourself for it? She said: Yes. He said: Go back, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No woman goes out to the mosque with her perfume diffusing but Allah Almighty accepts no prayer from her until she returns and washes."
"6389","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Malik, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Sufyan, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the sale of arayas for less than five wasqs, or for five wasqs; Dawud doubted whether five or less."
"6390","Suwayd narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Suhaym, freedman of Banu Zuhrah, who accompanied Abu Hurayrah, said: He heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An army will raid this House and be swallowed up in the desert."
"6391","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of one who hears wisdom then narrates the worst of what he heard is like a man who comes to a shepherd and says: Shepherd, sell me a sheep from your flock. He says: Go and take the best sheep by its ear. So he goes and takes the sheepdog by its ear."
"6392","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has pardoned for my Ummah what their souls whisper, so long as they do not speak of it or act upon it."
"6393","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has pardoned for my Ummah what their souls whisper, so long as they do not act upon it or speak of it."
"6394","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out until he came to the house of Fatimah, and I went out with him. He said: Is the little boy there? He said: He was kept back; I thought she was dressing him in a necklace or washing him. He said: Then he came, meaning al-Hasan, running; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced him and said: O Allah, I love him, so love him, and love whoever loves him."
"6395","Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to me, he said: Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, that he narrated to him, from Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best prayer after the obligatory is the night prayer."
"6396","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined. He said: Woe to you, what is that? He said: I had intercourse with my wife while fasting. He said: Free a slave. He said: I cannot find one. He said: Fast two consecutive months. He said: I cannot. He said: Feed sixty poor persons. He said: I cannot find. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket of dates and said: Take it and give it in charity. He said: Upon other than my family, O Messenger of Allah? By Allah, between the two lava plains of Madinah there is no household needier of it than mine. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his teeth appeared, and said: Take it, feed your family with it, and seek your Lord's forgiveness."
"6397","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, he said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every child is born upon the fitrah; his parents make him Jewish, Christian, or Magian."
"6398","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, in marfu' form, he said: He was asked: Which prayer is best after the obligatory, and which fasting is best after Ramadan? He said: The best prayer after the obligatory is prayer in the middle of the night, and the best fasting after Ramadan is the month of Allah, al-Muharram."
"6399","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Ubayd ibn Waqid al-Laythi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that Allah answer him in hardships and distress, let him supplicate abundantly in ease."
"6400","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr, meaning Ja'far ibn Iyas, narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that Allah answer him in hardships and distress, let him supplicate abundantly in ease."
"6401","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Truffles are from manna, their water is a cure for the eye, ajwah dates are from Paradise, and in them is a cure from poison."
"6402","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Khalid, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): After he spoke to Abd al-Qays about vessels what he spoke, he said: Drink whatever seems good to you; every man is accountable for himself."
"6403","With the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Truffles are a remnant of manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."
"6404","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to me, Abu Husayn narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for the rich, nor for the able-bodied strong."
"6405","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym ibn Irak ibn Malik narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Refrain for Allah's sake, refrain; were it not for humble youths, bowing elders, suckling infants, and grazing beasts, punishment would be poured upon you in torrents."
"6406","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from a shaykh of Banu Rabi'ah ibn Kilab, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A time will come upon people when a man is given the choice between incapacity and immorality; whoever reaches that, let him choose incapacity over immorality."
"6407","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Ashras narrating from Sayf, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Salih ibn Sarh, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not believe in the Decree, its good and its evil, I am free of him."
"6408","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Amr ibn al-Azraq, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a funeral with women weeping with it, and Umar ibn al-Khattab forbade them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave them, O son of al-Khattab, for the soul is afflicted, the eye is tearful, and the covenant is recent."
"6409","Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah Abu al-Muhajir, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Abu Hurayrah and Aishah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution three times three times."
"6410","Shayban narrated to us, Uqbah, meaning al-Asamm, al-Rifa'i narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disputed about truffles. Some said: I see it is the tree uprooted from above the earth with no stability. Some refrained from him, and that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Truffles are only from manna, their water is a cure for the eye, ajwah is from Paradise, and it is a cure from poison."
"6411","Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Isa ibn Abi Azzah, from Abu Thawr al-Azdi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to pray witr before I sleep. Isa said: Jabir used to pray witr at the beginning of the night, then sleep."
"6412","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Abi Abdullah, from Ya'qub ibn Salamah al-Laythi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer for one without ablution, and no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it."
"6413","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Ka'b, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are the radiant and white-limbed on the Day of Resurrection from the marks of ablution; whoever of you can extend his radiance, let him do so."
"6414","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Ka'b, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Imam says: Not of those who earned anger nor of those astray, and those behind him say: Amin, the Amin of the people of heaven and earth meet, and Allah forgives the servant what preceded of his sins. He said: The example of one who does not say: Amin is like a man who went raiding with a people and they cast lots; their arrows came out and his did not. He said: Why did my arrow not come out? He said: Because you did not say: Amin."
"6415","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from hunger, for it is an evil bedfellow; and I seek refuge in You from treachery, for it is an evil confidant, or: an evil mark."
"6416","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating at: When the sky is rent asunder."
"6417","Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Ammar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Ka'b, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Send abundant blessings upon me, for your blessings upon me are purification for you; and ask al-wasilah for me. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-wasilah? He said: The highest rank in Paradise, attained by only one man among people, and I hope I am he."
"6418","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Zakariyya Abu Amr al-Mada'ini narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Sa'id, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Salim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever licks honey three licks in every month will not be struck by a great calamity."
"6419","Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz, from Abu Hurayrah; and from the narration of Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If you say to your companion: Be silent, on Friday while the Imam is preaching, you have engaged in idle talk."
"6420","Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abbad, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Abu Salih al-Khawlani, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A group of my Ummah will keep fighting at the gates of Damascus and around it, and at the gates of Bayt al-Maqdis and around it; the forsaking of whoever forsakes them will not harm them, manifest upon the truth until the Hour comes."
"6421","Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Imran ibn Abi Anas narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, from Abu Hurayrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no believing man hate a believing woman; if he dislikes a trait in her, he is pleased with another."
"6422","Abdullah ibn Muti' narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, he said: Umar ibn al-Hakam informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no believing man hate a believing woman; if he dislikes a trait in her, he is pleased with another."
"6423","Muhammad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Harun and Musa ibn Abi Isa informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will it be with you, O people, when your women transgress and your youths are immoral? They said: O Messenger of Allah, will that really be? He said: Yes, and worse than it. How will it be with you when you abandon enjoining good and forbidding evil? They said: O Messenger of Allah, will that really be? He said: Yes, and worse than it. How will it be with you when you see evil as good and good as evil?"
"6424","Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: I heard Abu al-Jahm al-Qawwas narrating to my father, and he was a Persian man heavy of tongue, among the companions of Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A mine will appear in the land of Banu Sulaym called Pharaoh or Fir'an, and that in Abu al-Jahm's tongue is close to the same; the worst of people will go out to it, or: the worst of people will be gathered to it."
"6425","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Ismail, from his father, he said: My father used to pray behind Abu Hurayrah in Madinah, and his prayer was similar to that of Qays, completing bowing and prostration. It was said to Abu Hurayrah: Was this the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, and more complete."
"6426","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Yazid al-Awdi, from his father, he said: Abu Hurayrah entered the mosque and people gathered to him; a youth stood to him and said: I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomsoever I am his master, Ali is his master; O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him? He said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomsoever I am his master, Ali is his master; O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."
"6427","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was a tree narrowing the road, so a man cut it and removed it from the road, and he was forgiven."
"6428","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The eyes commit adultery, the hands commit adultery, the feet commit adultery, and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"6429","With the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Zakariyya was a carpenter."
"6430","With the same chain, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant obeys his master and obeys his Lord, he has two rewards."
"6431","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, I think from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever enters Paradise enjoys bliss and does not despair; his clothes do not wear out and his youth does not perish; in Paradise is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has not occurred to a human heart."
"6432","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah: A man used to pick up filth from the mosque, then died, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him. He said: What happened to so-and-so? They said: He died. He said: Did you not inform me of him? As if they belittled his affair. He said to his companions: Go, show me his grave. He went and prayed over him, then said: These graves are full of darkness upon their people, and Allah illuminates them for them by my prayer."
"6433","Hudbah and Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant remains in prayer so long as he awaits the prayer; the angels say: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, mercy him, until he leaves or breaks ablution."
"6434","With the same chain except Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abu Hurayrah: Pharaoh drove four stakes for his wife into her hands and feet; when they dispersed from her, the angels shaded her, and she said: My Lord, build for me with You a house in Paradise, and save me from Pharaoh and his deed, and save me from the wrongdoing people. Her house in Paradise was unveiled to her."
"6435","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: Qatadah narrated to us that Abu Rafi' narrated that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah wrote a book before creating creation: My mercy precedes My anger."
"6436","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I asked al-Hasan about fasting Friday, and he said: It is forbidden except in consecutive days. He said: Abu Rafi' narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting Friday except in days before it or after it."
"6437","Abu Ma'mar Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abu Rafi', he said: I prayed the last Isha behind Abu Hurayrah, and we prostrated at: When the sky is rent asunder. When he finished his prayer I said: Do you prostrate at: When the sky is rent asunder? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer and prostrated in it, so I shall keep prostrating in it."
"6438","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Mihran, Abu Rafi' narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in prayer, let him not spit toward the qiblah nor to his right, but beneath his left foot; if he cannot, let him spit into the edge of his garment, then fold part over part. Abu Hurayrah said: As if I see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) folding his garment part over part."
"6439","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Qatadah, that Abu Rafi' narrated from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: They dig every day until they almost see the sun's rays, then say: We will return to it tomorrow; they return and it is stronger than ever. When their term reaches and Allah Almighty wills to send them upon people, they say: We will return to it tomorrow, if Allah wills; they return to it as they left it and dig through it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People flee from them into their fortresses. Al-Mu'tamir said: My father said, from Qatadah: They shoot arrows at the sky, which return to them with blood, and they say: We have overcome the earth and subdued the people of heaven. He said: Allah sends upon them worms in their necks that kill them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even their beasts grow fat and exultant from eating their flesh."
"6440","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Khilas, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer has two wives; the marrow of their shins is seen through their garments."
"6441","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Adhrami narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Khilas, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Two men disputed over a sale with no proof between them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to cast lots for the oath, whether they liked or disliked."
"6442","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Khilas, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are followers of Quraysh: their disbelievers follow their disbelievers, and their Muslims follow their Muslims."
"6443","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Musa narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: Abu Hurayrah informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you rises from sleep, let him pour water over his right hand three times before putting it in, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"6444","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi al-Husayn narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Hurayrah informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was sleeping, I saw two gold bangles on my hands; their affair concerned me, so I blew on them and they flew away. I interpreted them as two liars who will emerge after me; it was revealed to me: Blow them away. So I blew them and they flew; I interpreted them as two liars emerging after me. One was al-Ansi, master of Sanaa, and the other Musaylimah."
"6445","Ibrahim ibn Ar'arah narrated to us, Ma'n ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Amr, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is punished by the weeping of the living."
"6446","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits it, the thief does not steal while he is a believer when he steals, and he does not drink wine while he is a believer when he drinks it."
"6447","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, from Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The testimony of the bedouin against the townsman is not accepted."
"6448","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Abdah informed us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah has one hundred mercies: one among mankind, jinn, beasts, and vermin, in which they show affection and mercy, and by which wild beasts are tender to their young; and He kept ninety-nine by which He will mercy His servants on the Day of Resurrection."
"6449","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Kulthum ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sidrah narrated to us, that Ata al-Khurasani narrated to them from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Part of the excellence of prayer is lengthening the standing."
"6450","Abu Yasir narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Hurayrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Suhur is blessing, tharid is blessing, and congregation is blessing."
"6451","Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me: Umar entered the mosque while the Abyssinians were playing and rebuked them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave them, for they are the sons of Arfidah."
"6452","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Abu Murrah, freedman of Aqil, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Two ravenous hungry wolves among sheep that scattered, one at its front and the other at its rear, are not quicker in corruption than a man in his religion who loves worldly honor and wealth."
"6453","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ma'di ibn Sulayman Abu Sulayman, keeper of food, narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps one of you takes sheep and stays at a mountain top, a mile or two from Madinah; Friday comes and he does not attend congregation, then another Friday comes and he does not attend, so his heart is sealed and he becomes among the heedless."
"6454","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The nobility of the believer is his piety, his manliness is his intellect, his lineage is his religion; cowardice and boldness are instincts Allah Almighty places where He wills. The coward flees from his own father and mother, while the bold fights for what he does not care never to return with to his family."
"6455","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays Fajr is under Allah Almighty's protection; let not Allah pursue you for His protection. Whoever kills a covenanted person under Allah's and His Messenger's protection has betrayed Allah Almighty's protection; he will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, whose fragrance is found from seventy years' journey."
"6456","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ma'di narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Whoever announces a funeral and then leaves it to return to his family has a qirat; if he accompanies it he has a qirat; if he prays over it he has a qirat; and if he sits until its burial is completed he has a qirat. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A qirat with Allah is like Mount Uhud, or: greater than Mount Uhud."
"6457","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prayer in which the Mother of the Quran is not recited is deficient, deficient, deficient, incomplete. They said: O Abu Hurayrah, what if I am behind the imam? He said: Recite it within yourself, O Persian."
"6458","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, that he attended a funeral and Marwan ibn al-Hakam led the prayer over it. Then Abu Hurayrah went until we sat at the burial ground, and Abu Sa'id came and said to Marwan: Show me your hand. He gave him his hand and he said: Stand. So he stood. Then Marwan said: Why did you make me stand? He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a funeral he would stand until it was carried past, and he said: Death is a terror. Marwan said: Is it true, Abu Hurayrah? He said: Yes. He said: What prevented you from telling me? He said: You were the imam; you sat, so I sat."
"6459","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yawning is from Satan, so when one of you yawns let him suppress it as much as he can."
"6460","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man dies his deeds are cut off except from three: except from an ongoing charity, or knowledge that is benefited from, or a righteous child who supplicates for him."
"6461","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity does not decrease wealth, and Allah does not increase a servant through pardon except in honor, and no one humbles himself for Allah except that Allah raises him."
"6462","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The False Messiah will come from the east with his aim set on Madinah, until he descends behind Uhud; then the angels will turn his face toward Syria, and there he will perish."
"6463","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A false oath sells the goods but wipes out the earnings."
"6464","Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to me, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw in a dream as if the sons of al-Hakam were leaping onto his pulpit and coming down. In the morning he was as if angered, and said: Why is it that I saw the sons of al-Hakam leaping onto my pulpit like monkeys leap? He said: After that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never seen laughing heartily until he died, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"6465","Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Muslim, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cursed is the one who approaches women in their backs."
"6466","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: When one of you prays and then sits in the place where he prayed, the angels continue to pray for him: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him, so long as he does not break his ablution or stand up."
"6467","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Madini narrated to us - and he was better than his father, Allah willing - al-Ala narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Ja'far ibn Abi Talib as an angel flying with the angels on two wings in Paradise."
"6468","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il and others said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever."
"6469","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, meaning that Allah Almighty says: I asked My servant for a loan and he did not lend Me, and My servant reviled Me without knowing, saying: O age, O age - and I am Time."
"6470","Hashim ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah al-Kufi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Ala al-Razi, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the procrastinating woman and the woman who falsely claims menstruation. As for the procrastinating woman: when her husband desires her, she says: Later, right now. And as for the one who falsely claims menstruation: when her husband desires her, she says: I am menstruating, while she is not menstruating."
"6471","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Ala narrating from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun has neither risen nor set upon a day better than Friday. There is no creature except that it is terrified of Friday except these two heavy creations of jinn and men. At every gate of the mosque there are two angels writing down who came first, first: like a man who offered a camel, like a man who offered a cow, like a man who offered a sheep, and like a man who offered a chicken or a bird. When the imam comes out, the angels sit and listen to the remembrance, and the scrolls are folded."
"6472","Ahmad ibn Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek trustworthiness among Quraysh, for the trustworthy man of Quraysh has merit over the trustworthy man of others, and the strong man of Quraysh has merit over the strong man of others."
"6473","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever finds the very substance of his property with a man who has become bankrupt has more right to it than any other of the creditors."
"6474","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the most noble of people? He said: The most God-fearing of them toward Allah. They said: It is not about this that we ask you... the hadith."
"6475","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Sakhr, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever comes to this mosque of mine, coming only for some good to learn it or teach it, is like the fighter in the path of Allah; and whoever comes for anything else is like a man looking at another's merchandise."
"6476","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Sakhr, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent out a detachment, and they took great spoils and returned swiftly. Then a man said... the hadith."
"6477","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from Abu Talhah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images. He said: So we said: Let us go to Aishah. We told her what Abu Talhah had said, and she said: I do not know, but I will tell you what I saw him do. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on one of his expeditions, and I was awaiting his return. I took a patterned cloth of ours and screened the bridal chamber with it. When he approached, I stood and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah; praise be to Allah who has honored you and granted you victory and ennobled you. She said: He raised his head and looked at the cloth but did not return anything to me, and I recognized displeasure on his face. He went on until he tore down the cloth, then said: O Aishah, Allah has not commanded us, in what He has provided us, to clothe stones and bricks. She said: So I took it and made it into a cushion stuffed with palm fiber, and he did not fault me for that."
"6478","Ibrahim ibn Dinar narrated to us, Abu Qatan narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Khilas, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If people knew what is in the first row, it would have to be decided by drawing lots."
"6479","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq al-Sabi'i narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Abu Rafi', who said: I prayed the evening prayer with Abu Hurayrah, and he recited: When the sky splits asunder. I said something to him about it, and he said: Abu al-Qasim, peace be upon him, prostrated for it while I was with him. Al-Taymi said - or he said: I prostrated for it with Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and I shall continue to prostrate for it until I meet Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"6480","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Damrah narrated to us, from Ibn Ata, from his father, who said: Abu Hurayrah visited his people and they brought him thin bread of the finest thin bread. When he saw it, he wept. It was said to him: What makes you weep, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never saw this with his own eyes."
"6481","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: New moons would pass over the household of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without a lamp being lit in any of their houses nor a fire being kindled in it; if they found oil they would anoint themselves with it, and if they found fat they would eat it."
"6482","Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ubayd ibn Abi Ubayd, the freedman of Abu Ruhm, who said: I was walking with Abu Hurayrah to the mosque when a perfumed woman passed by him, her scent wafting. He said to her: Where are you going, O maidservant of the Almighty? She said: To the mosque. He said: And did you perfume yourself for it? She said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any woman who perfumes herself for this mosque in order to go out to it, no prayer of hers is accepted until she washes from it as she washes from major impurity."
"6483","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A false oath sells the goods but wipes out the profit."
"6484","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two who revile each other - whatever they say is upon the one who began, so long as the wronged one does not transgress."
"6485","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ja'far narrated to us, saying: Al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - and Ubayy ibn Ka'b recited the Mother of the Quran to him - and he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, Allah has not sent down in the Torah, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Psalms, nor in the Criterion anything like it; it is indeed the Seven Oft-Repeated and the Mighty Quran which I have been given."
"6486","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard against the two things that bring curses. They said: What are the two things that bring curses, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The one who relieves himself on people's road or in their shade."
"6487","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was walking on a road in a fine suit of his, his self and his cloak pleased him, so the earth swallowed him, and he keeps sinking into the earth until the Day of Resurrection."
"6488","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was walking on a road he spotted a branch of thorns and said: By Allah, I shall surely remove this so it does not strike any of the Muslims. He removed it, and Allah forgave him."
"6489","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The five prayers, and Friday to Friday, are expiation for what is between them, so long as major sins are not committed."
"6490","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one of my nation endures the hardship and severity of Madinah except that I shall be his intercessor on the Day of Resurrection - or: a witness for him."
"6491","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan cannot take my likeness."
"6492","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever calls to guidance shall have a reward like the rewards of those who follow him, without decreasing anything from their rewards; and whoever calls to misguidance shall bear sin like the sins of those who follow him, without decreasing anything from their sins."
"6493","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He whose neighbor is not safe from his harms shall not enter Paradise."
"6494","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been favored over the prophets with six: I have been given the concise comprehensive speech, I have been aided with terror, spoils have been made lawful for me, the earth has been made for me a means of purification and a place of prayer, I have been sent to all creation, and the prophets have been sealed with me."
"6495","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, with the same chain, similarly."
"6496","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, saying: Al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what backbiting is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Your mentioning your brother with what he dislikes. It was said: What if what I say is in my brother? He said: If what you say is in him, you have backbitten him; and if it is not in him, you have slandered him."
"6497","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My father died and left wealth but made no bequest; will it expiate for him if I give charity on his behalf? He said: Yes."
"6498","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah sends blessings upon him ten times."
"6499","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you supplicates, let him not say: O Allah, forgive me if You will; rather let him be firm and make his desire great, for nothing Allah gives is too great for Allah Almighty."
"6500","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call for prayer is made, do not come to it while rushing; come to it with tranquility upon you. Whatever you catch, pray it, and whatever you miss, complete it. For when one of you heads toward prayer, he is in prayer."
"6501","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun neither rises nor sets upon a day better than Friday. There is no creature except that it is terrified of Friday except these two heavy creations of jinn and men. At every gate of the mosque there are two angels writing down the first, first: like a man who offered a camel, like a man who offered a cow, like a man who offered a sheep, like a man who offered a bird, and like a man who offered an egg. When the imam sits, the scrolls are folded."
"6502","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know who the bankrupt is? They said: The bankrupt among us is the one who has neither dirham nor goods. He said: The bankrupt of my nation is the one who comes on the Day of Resurrection with prayer, fasting and charity, but comes having insulted this one, slandered this one, consumed the wealth of this one, shed the blood of this one, and struck this one. So this one is settled from his good deeds and this one from his good deeds. If his good deeds run out before what is upon him is settled, their sins are taken and cast upon him, then he is cast into the Fire."
"6503","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: When My servant intends a good deed and does not do it, I record it for him as a good deed; if he does it, I record it for him as ten good deeds up to seven hundredfold. And when My servant intends an evil deed and does not do it, I do not record it against him; if he does it, I record it against him as one evil deed."
"6504","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The eyes commit adultery, the tongue commits adultery, and the feet commit adultery; the private part confirms that or denies it."
"6505","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the graveyard and said: Peace be upon you, O abode of a believing people; and we, Allah willing, shall join you. I wish we had seen our brothers. They said: Are we not your brothers, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Rather you are my companions; our brothers are those who have not yet come. They said: How will you know those of your nation who have not yet come, O Messenger of Allah? He said: What do you think - if a man had horses with white blazes on their foreheads and white marks on their legs among horses that are jet black, would he not recognize his horses? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They will come with white blazes from ablution, and I shall precede them at the Basin. Some shall surely be driven away from my Basin as the stray camel is driven away. I shall call to them: Come, come! Then it will be said: They changed after you. So I shall say: Away, away!"
"6506","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to that by which Allah wipes out sins and raises ranks? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Perfecting ablution despite hardships, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for one prayer after another prayer; that is the guarding of the frontier."
"6507","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right of a Muslim over a Muslim is six. He said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: When you meet him, greet him with peace; when he invites you, accept his invitation; when he seeks your advice, advise him; when he sneezes and praises Allah Almighty, ask Allah to have mercy on him; when he falls ill, visit him; and when he dies, follow his funeral."
"6508","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A disbeliever and his killer shall never be gathered together in the Fire."
"6509","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: my male slave and my female slave; all of you are slaves of Allah and all your women are maidservants of Allah. Rather let him say: my boy, my girl, my young man and my young woman."
"6510","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the believer knew what punishment is with Allah Almighty, no one would hope for His Paradise; and if the disbeliever knew what mercy is with Allah, no one would despair of His Paradise."
"6511","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion, no hamah, no rain-star influence, and no Safar."
"6512","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah created one hundred mercies; He placed one among His creation and kept ninety-nine with Him."
"6513","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is Yemeni, and disbelief is toward the east; tranquility is among the people of sheep, and pride and showing off are among the loud-voiced owners of horses and camels."
"6514","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour shall not come until thirty impostors emerge, each of them claiming to be the Messenger of Allah; and until knowledge is taken away, tribulations appear, and harj increases. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is harj? He said: Killing."
"6515","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no disease except that in the black seed there is a cure for it, except death."
"6516","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rights shall surely be restored to their owners on the Day of Resurrection, until the hornless sheep is retaliated for against the horned sheep."
"6517","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A Muslim shall not outbid his brother, nor propose marriage over his proposal."
"6518","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten to deeds before tribulations like portions of the dark night: a man wakes a believer and sleeps a disbeliever, and sleeps a believer and wakes a disbeliever, selling his religion for a portion of this world."
"6519","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten to deeds before six: the rising of the sun from its west, or the False Messiah, or the Smoke, or the Beast, or the private affair of one of you, or the general affair."
"6520","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Hour shall not come until the sun rises from its west; when it rises from its west, all people together shall believe. Then on that day no soul shall benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith."
"6521","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two who revile each other - whatever they say is upon the one who began, so long as the wronged one does not transgress."
"6522","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bells are the pipes of Satan."
"6523","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a heap of food, put his hand into it, and his fingers felt wetness. He said: What is this, O owner of the food? He said: Rain struck it, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Why did you not put it on top of the food so people could see it? Whoever cheats me is not of me."
"6524","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: Fix prices, O Messenger of Allah. He said: It is Allah who raises and lowers; I hope to meet Allah without anyone having a claim of injustice against me. Another said to him: Fix prices. He said: I shall supplicate to Allah Almighty."
"6525","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays a prayer and does not recite in it the Mother of the Quran, it is deficient, deficient, deficient, incomplete."
"6526","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: When the sons of Abi al-As reach thirty, the religion of Allah becomes a means of exploitation, the wealth of Allah becomes something passed around, and the servants of Allah become subjugated."
"6527","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, saying: Al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was building the mosque; when the people carried one stone, Ammar would carry two stones, and when they carried one brick, he would carry two bricks. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to Ibn Sumayyah; the rebellious party shall kill him."
"6528","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred House."
"6529","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever."
"6530","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends blessings upon me once, ten good deeds are recorded for him thereby."
"6531","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about backbiting and said: That you say of your brother what he dislikes; if you are truthful you have backbitten him, and if you are lying you have slandered him."
"6532","With the same chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: my male slave and my female slave; all of you are slaves of Allah, and all your women are maidservants of Allah. Rather let him say: my young man, my boy, my girl."
"6533","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me has indeed seen me, for Satan cannot take my form."
"6534","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Mother of the Quran is among the Seven Oft-Repeated which I was given - as if he meant the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6535","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, saying: Al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about backbiting. He said: Your mentioning your brother with what he dislikes. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what if what I say is in my brother? He said: If it is in him, you have backbitten him; and if what you say is not in him, you have slandered him."
"6536","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sign of the hypocrite is three, even if he fasts and prays and claims to be a Muslim: when he speaks he lies, when he is trusted he betrays, and when he promises he breaks his promise."
"6537","With the chain, Abu al-Qasim Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed us: Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Janzarudhi informed us; Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdun ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Sinan, the jurist, informed us, read to him in Jumada al-Akhirah in the year 375; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in what he narrates from his Lord Almighty, He said: My servant committed a sin and said: My Lord, forgive me my sin. Then the Blessed and Exalted said: My servant committed a sin and knew he has a Lord who forgives sins and seizes for sins. Then he returned and committed a sin and said: My Lord, forgive me my sin. Then the Blessed and Exalted said: My servant committed a sin and knew he has a Lord who forgives sins and seizes for sins. Do as you wish, for I have forgiven you."
"6538","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three, Allah's help for each of them is a right upon Allah: the fighter in the path of Allah, the contracted slave who seeks to pay, and the one who marries seeking chastity."
"6539","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from an evil neighbor in the permanent abode, for the neighbor of the desert moves away."
"6540","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Among the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, from a supplication that is not heard, from a heart that does not humble itself, and from a soul that is never satisfied."
"6541","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man asked him: How many handfuls shall I pour over my head while I am in major impurity? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pour three handfuls over his head. The man said: My hair is long? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had more hair than you and better."
"6542","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on a servant who had an injustice against his brother regarding honor or wealth, and sought his pardon before it is taken from him when there is neither dinar nor dirham; if he has good deeds, they are taken from his good deeds, and if he has no good deeds, their evil deeds are placed upon him."
"6543","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you prostrates, let him begin with his knees before his hands, and let him not kneel as the stallion kneels."
"6544","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If the slave-girl of one of you commits adultery and her adultery becomes evident, let him flog her the prescribed penalty without reproach; then if she commits adultery again, let him flog her without reproach; then if she commits adultery again, let him flog her without reproach; then if she commits adultery again, let him sell her even for a rope."
"6545","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you awaits except enriching wealth that transgresses, or impoverishing poverty that makes forget, or a debilitating illness, or a sudden death, or the False Messiah - and the False Messiah is the worst awaited absent - or the Hour, and the Hour is more calamitous and more bitter."
"6546","Abu Musa Ishaq ibn Musa ibn Abd Allah ibn Musa ibn Yazid al-Ansari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl ibn Sulayman, the freedman of Banu Makhzum, narrated to me, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The battlefield of deaths is between sixty and seventy."
"6547","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fewest of my nation are the children of seventy years."
"6548","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he strove hard, would say: O Living, O Sustainer."
"6549","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a matter weighed upon him, would look to the sky and say: Glory be to Allah the Magnificent."
"6550","Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Ruzayni narrated to us, saying: I never saw his like with my eyes; Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from a man, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When Thumamah became Muslim, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to wash and pray two units."
"6551","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode to Majma' al-Suyul and said: Shall I not tell you of the False Messiah's position relative to Madinah? He said: This is his place; he will aim for Madinah but shall not be able to reach it; at every pass of its passes there is an angel brandishing his weapon; the False Messiah shall not enter it. It is with me in another place more complete than this."
"6552","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes on Friday, wears the best of his clothes, and goes early until he arrives, then listens and is silent, is forgiven what is between it and the next Friday. He said: I narrated this to Abu Bakr Amr ibn Hazm, and he said: With an addition of four days."
"6553","Ahmad ibn Imran al-Akhnasi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You shall never encompass people with your wealth, but cheerfulness of face from you shall encompass them."
"6554","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, saying: Amr informed me, from Abu Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a fasting person has nothing from his fasting but hunger and thirst, and how many a night-praying person has nothing from his standing but sleeplessness."
"6555","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah says: I am the most self-sufficient of partners from association; whoever does a deed and associates another with Me in it, I am free of it."
"6556","With the same chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent from the best generations of the sons of Adam, generation after generation, until I was sent from the generation in which I was."
"6557","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."
"6558","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from al-Agharr, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise."
"6559","Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his health and hardiness pleased him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When did you last feel Umm Mildam? The Bedouin said: What is Umm Mildam? He said: Fever. He said: What is fever? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: A heat between the skin and the bone. The Bedouin said: I have never had that. He said to him: When did you last feel headache? He said: What is headache? He said to him: A throbbing in the temples and the head. He said: I have never had that. When the Bedouin turned away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man of the people of the Fire, let him look at him - meaning the Bedouin."
"6560","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Quran has a period of eagerness, and people have a period of slackness from it; whoever's slackness is toward moderation, blessed is it, and whoever's slackness is toward turning away, those are the ruined ones."
"6561","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, that Abu Basrah Humayl ibn Basrah met Abu Hurayrah while he was coming from the Mount, and said: Had I met you before you went to it, you would not have gone to it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The camels' livers are beaten only toward three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Furthest Mosque."
"6562","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Sakhr, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent out a detachment and they took great spoils and returned swiftly. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we never saw a detachment swifter in return nor greater in spoils than this detachment. He said: Shall I not tell you of one swifter in return than it and greater in spoils? A man who performs ablution in his house and perfects it, then sets out to the mosque and prays the dawn prayer in it, then follows it with the forenoon prayer - he has returned more swiftly and with greater spoils."
"6563","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite the Quran correctly and seek its rare expressions."
"6564","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih al-Tammar al-Madini narrated to us, Muslim ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, who said: We were with Abu Hurayrah when al-Hasan ibn Ali came, greeted, and we returned his greeting while Abu Hurayrah did not know. He passed on, and we said: O Abu Hurayrah, this is al-Hasan ibn Ali greeting us. He followed him and caught up with him, and said: Peace be upon you, my master. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He is a master."
"6565","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which people are the most noble? He said: The most noble of them with Allah Almighty are the most God-fearing. They said: It is other than this that we ask you about, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then the most noble of people is Yusuf, son of a prophet of Allah, son of a prophet of Allah, son of the intimate friend of Allah. They said: Yes. He said: The best of them in the pre-Islamic age are the best of them in Islam, when they understand."
"6566","Al-Ashajj narrated to us, Uqbah and Abu Usamah narrated to us, saying: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity due from a man on his horse nor on his slave."
"6567","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Uqbah narrated to us, saying: Usamah narrated to me, saying: Makhul narrated to me, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"6568","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you intends the greeting, let him say: Peace be upon you, for Allah is Peace; and do not begin with anything before Allah."
"6569","Sahl ibn Zanjalah narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us; I heard Ibn Ajlan mentioning, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to a gathering, let him greet; and if he stands to leave, let him greet; the first is no more deserving than the last."
"6570","Sahl narrated to us, al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, similarly, but he did not mention his father."
"6571","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Talhah ibn Abi Sa'id informed me, that Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to him from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever keeps a horse in the path of Allah out of faith and belief in Allah's promise, its feed, its drink, its urine and its dung shall be good deeds in his scale on the Day of Resurrection."
"6572","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a funeral and they praised it with good, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. Then another funeral was carried past him and they praised it with evil, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. Then he said: You are Allah's witnesses on earth."
"6573","Suwayd narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no ruler over ten except that he shall be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand chained to his neck until justice frees him or tyranny destroys him."
"6574","Suwayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord Almighty says: Three, I am their adversary, and whoever I am his adversary I shall defeat him: a man who gives a pledge by Me then betrays, a man who sells a free man and consumes his price, and a man who hires a worker, takes full service from him, and does not pay him his wage."
"6575","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is appointed only to be followed; when he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he prostrates, prostrate; when he rises, rise; when he sits, sit; and when he stands, stand. The imam is a shield, guaranteeing the prayer of the people. If he prays it in its time and observes its limits - I think he said - he shall have his reward and the like of their rewards, without decreasing anything from their rewards; and whoever does not pray it in its time nor observe its limits shall bear its sin and their sins, and nothing shall be upon them."
"6576","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to us, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."
"6577","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to us, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah is Peace, so do not begin with anything before Him; when it is said: Peace be upon you, say: Peace be upon you."
"6578","Jubarah narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has creatures whom He spreads under the night as He wills; so tie the mouths of waterskins, close the doors, and cover vessels, for it opens no door, uncovers no cover, and unties no knot."
"6579","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah."
"6580","And from his uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Yasar, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would delay the last evening prayer to a third of the night; for when the first third of the night passes, Allah Almighty descends to the lowest heaven and remains there until dawn rises, saying: Is there a repentant one? Is there a asker to be given? Is there a supplicant to be answered? Is there a sinner seeking forgiveness to be forgiven? Is there a sick one seeking healing to be healed?"
"6581","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque, and a man entered and prayed as he prayed, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned his greeting and said: Go back and pray, for you have not prayed - until he did that three times. The man said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I know nothing better than this; teach me. He said: When you stand for prayer, say the takbir, then recite what is easy for you of the Quran, then bow until you are tranquil while bowing, then rise until you stand upright, then prostrate until you are tranquil while prostrating, then rise until you are tranquil standing, then do that throughout your prayer."
"6582","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women are married for four: for their wealth, their lineage, their beauty, and their religion; so win the religious one, may your hands be dusty."
"6583","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of the desert people gave me a she-camel of his camels as a gift, and I compensated him with six young she-camels. He remained that day displeased. By Allah, after this day of mine I shall accept no gift except from a Qurashi, or a Thaqafi, or a Dawsi, or an Ansari."
"6584","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Rafi', from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah created Adam from dust, then made him clay, then left him until he was altered black mud; He created him and fashioned him, then left him until he was dry clay like pottery. Iblis would pass by him and say: You have surely been created for a great matter. Then Allah breathed His spirit into him; the first thing the spirit reached was his sight and his nostrils. He sneezed, and Allah taught him to praise his Lord. The Lord said: May your Lord have mercy on you. Then Allah said: O Adam, go to that group, greet them, and see what they say. He came and greeted them, and they said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. He came back to his Lord, who said: What did they say to you - while He knew best what they said to him. He said: My Lord, when I greeted them, they said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. He said: O Adam, this is your greeting and the greeting of your offspring. He said: My Lord, what is my offspring? He said: Choose My hand, O Adam. He said: I choose the right hand of my Lord - and both hands of my Lord are right. Allah spread His palm, and there was every one of his offspring that would ever be in the palm of the Merciful Almighty: men among them with light upon their mouths, and a man whose light amazed Adam. He said: My Lord, who is this? He said: Your son Dawud. He said: My Lord, how much life have You made for him? He said: I made for him sixty. He said: My Lord, complete for him from my life until his life is a hundred years. Allah did so and called witnesses to that. When Adam's life ran out, Allah sent the Angel of Death to him. Adam said: Has there not remained forty years of my life? The angel said: Did you not give it to your son Dawud? He denied that, so his offspring denied; and he forgot, so his offspring forgot."
"6585","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Abd Allah al-Qurashi, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there an hour of the night and day that you command me not to pray in? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray dawn, refrain from prayer until the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of Satan; then prayer is witnessed, attended and accepted until midday. When midday comes, refrain from prayer until the sun declines - he said: at that time Hell is stoked, and the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell. When the sun declines, prayer is attended, witnessed and accepted until you pray the afternoon; when you pray the afternoon, refrain from prayer until the sun sets; then prayer is witnessed, attended and accepted until you pray dawn."
"6586","Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ma'n narrated to me, saying: My father narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The grateful eater is like the patient fasting person."
"6587","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Usamah, from Ubayd ibn Nistas, the freedman of Kathir ibn al-Salt - he narrated to him - from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, wealth is not from abundance of goods; rather wealth is wealth of soul. Allah Almighty fulfills for His servant what He has written for him of sustenance, so be wholesome in seeking: take what is lawful and leave what is unlawful."
"6588","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Abu Sakhr, that Sa'id al-Maqburi informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, Jesus son of Mary shall surely descend as a just imam and a fair judge; he shall break the cross, kill the pig, mend relations, remove hatred, and wealth shall be offered to him and he shall not accept it. Then if he stands at my grave and says: O Muhammad, I shall surely answer him."
"6589","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Amr informed me, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the dawn prayer one day and came to the women in the mosque and stood over them and said: O assembly of women, I have never seen any deficient in mind and religion more overpowering to the hearts of men of understanding than you; and I have seen that you shall be most of the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, so draw near to Allah Almighty with whatever you can. Among the women was the wife of Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud. She went to Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud and told him what she heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and took some jewelry of hers. Ibn Mas'ud said: Where are you going with this jewelry? She said: I draw near with it to Allah Almighty and His Messenger, peace be upon him, that Allah may not make me of the people of the Fire. He said: Come, woe to you; give it in charity to me and my children, for we are a place for it. She said: No, by Allah, until I go with it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She went to seek permission to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: This is Zaynab seeking permission, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Which of the Zaynabs is she? He said: The wife of Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud. He said: Admit her. She entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard a statement from you, and I returned to Ibn Mas'ud and told him, and I took jewelry to draw near with it to Allah Almighty and to you, hoping Allah would not make me of the people of the Fire. Ibn Mas'ud said to me: Give it in charity to me and my sons, for we are a place for it. I said: Until I seek permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give it in charity to his sons and to him, for they are a place for it. Then she said: O Messenger of Allah, what about what I heard from you when you stood over us: I have never seen any deficient in mind ever nor in religion more overpowering to the hearts of men of understanding than you - O Messenger of Allah, what is the deficiency of our religion and our minds? He said: As for what I mentioned of the deficiency of your religion: the menstruation that befalls you; one of you remains as long as Allah wills her to remain, neither praying nor fasting - that is the deficiency of your religion. And as for what I mentioned of the deficiency of your minds: the testimony of a woman is half a testimony."
"6590","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the Day of Resurrection, the angels and the prophets shall intercede, until it is said to one of them: Whoever had the weight of a dinar in his heart; then it is said: half a dinar; then it is said: a qirat; then it is said: half a qirat; then it is said: a barley grain; then it is said: a mustard seed. When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, the Almighty says: The creation has interceded for the creation, and the mercy of the Creator remains. He said: So He takes a handful from Hell and casts it into the River of Life. He said: They sprout as plants sprout - have you not seen the seed in the flood-borne soil? What of it was in the open is green, and what of it was in the shade is white. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is as if you were looking at the seed as it sprouts. He said: Then they enter Paradise. He said: It is said: These are the freed ones of the Merciful."
"6591","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Some poor people came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the people of wealth and riches have taken this world and the Hereafter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was startled and said: How is that? They said: They have wealth from which they give charity while we have no wealth; they have wealth from which they fight while we have no wealth; and they have wealth from which they perform pilgrimage while we have no wealth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you of something by which you can catch up with their deeds? Glorify Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times; you shall catch up with their deeds. They did that, and the wealthy heard of it and did the like of their deeds. They said: O Messenger of Allah, they have said the like of what we said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is the bounty of Allah; He gives it to whom He wills."
"6592","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah."
"6593","And from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to trim the mustaches and leave the beards."
"6594","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What is perfecting ablution? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent until prayer time came. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water, washed his hands, rinsed his nose and mouth, washed his face three times, his arms three times each, wiped his head, washed his feet three times each, then sprinkled beneath his garment, and said: Such is perfecting ablution."
"6595","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq al-Madini, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; his due hospitality is three days, and what is beyond that is charity; and it is not lawful for him to stay with him until he forces him out."
"6596","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not love wasting wealth, nor excessive asking, nor hearsay."
"6597","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, with the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Two men sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of them nobler than the other. One of them sneezed and praised Allah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Allah to have mercy on him. Then the other sneezed but did not praise Allah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not ask mercy for him. The noble one said: This one sneezed and you asked mercy for him, while I sneezed and you did not ask mercy for me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He remembered Allah so I remembered him, while you forgot - meaning Allah - so I forgot you."
"6598","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every son of Adam is born upon the natural disposition; then his parents make him a Jew and make him a Christian."
"6599","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be straight, draw near, and receive glad tidings; seek help in the early morning, the late afternoon, and something of the night journey; upon you is moderation and you shall reach. Know that none of you shall be saved by his deeds. We said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah Almighty envelops me with mercy and bounty from Him."
"6600","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five are of the natural disposition: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, plucking the armpit, trimming the mustache, and clipping the nails."
